WEBVTT

1
00:00:06,006 --> 00:00:09,175
[whimsical ethereal music playing]

2
00:00:21,312 --> 00:00:24,024
{\an8}[people chattering]

3
00:00:35,201 --> 00:00:37,746
{\an8}[Alejandra] <i>I always dreamed</i>
<i>about being a mom.</i>

4
00:00:37,829 --> 00:00:40,457
{\an8}<i>I got married when I was 17</i>
<i>and full of hope.</i>

5
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:44,419
{\an8}<i>I was pregnant which was partially</i>
<i>why we decided to get married.</i>

6
00:00:44,502 --> 00:00:46,921
{\an8}<i>But I've always loved Arturo.</i>

7
00:00:48,339 --> 00:00:50,383
I've always liked children.

8
00:00:51,676 --> 00:00:54,304
I've always been drawn to them.

9
00:00:54,929 --> 00:00:57,432
And all the kids in my family,

10
00:00:58,433 --> 00:00:59,726
they…

11
00:00:59,809 --> 00:01:03,855
They, mm, have always
been very attached to me though.

12
00:01:03,938 --> 00:01:05,648
My family is pretty big.

13
00:01:05,732 --> 00:01:08,359
My family has… well they,
all have children, you know?

14
00:01:08,443 --> 00:01:10,653
All my cousins have children.

15
00:01:11,362 --> 00:01:12,655
So I…

16
00:01:12,739 --> 00:01:16,993
So I like the idea
of just me being a mom. Yeah, so, um…

17
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:21,706
It was like, like fulfilling my dream
of having a family.

18
00:01:21,790 --> 00:01:26,753
Since I got pregnant and we got married,
that was always our plan.

19
00:01:26,836 --> 00:01:28,922
I always, always saw myself as a mom.

20
00:01:29,005 --> 00:01:30,840
[director] Cut. Great. I love it.

21
00:01:30,924 --> 00:01:33,009
Can we try a version that's more fluid?

22
00:01:33,093 --> 00:01:35,970
The text you're going to read
is from an interview we have to emulate,

23
00:01:36,054 --> 00:01:38,848
and the character you would have to play

24
00:01:38,932 --> 00:01:41,643
-is Ale, from 15 years ago.
-[actress] Mm.

25
00:01:41,726 --> 00:01:44,437
-Like a flashback that the actress has…
-[actress] Yeah.

26
00:01:44,521 --> 00:01:46,231
about the real Ale, okay?

27
00:01:46,314 --> 00:01:48,608
[quiet dramatic music playing]

28
00:01:51,194 --> 00:01:53,780
-[woman] Casting, 1F, take one.
-[man] Mark.

29
00:01:57,075 --> 00:01:58,868
I wanted it so bad, you know?

30
00:02:00,411 --> 00:02:04,999
And… I found myself
in all these complicated situations.

31
00:02:06,167 --> 00:02:07,877
So I began to make

32
00:02:08,837 --> 00:02:10,547
some choices

33
00:02:10,630 --> 00:02:14,801
which caused things to start getting
even more complicated.

34
00:02:16,970 --> 00:02:18,680
Until there was nowhere to go.

35
00:02:19,806 --> 00:02:21,891
I was in over my head.

36
00:02:21,975 --> 00:02:24,853
[whimsical ethereal music playing]

37
00:02:24,936 --> 00:02:30,817
A CHILD OF MY OWN

38
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:32,193
[camera shutter clicks]

39
00:02:32,735 --> 00:02:33,862
[photographer] Very good.

40
00:02:33,945 --> 00:02:35,363
[camera whirring]

41
00:02:35,446 --> 00:02:36,698
That's it.

42
00:02:36,781 --> 00:02:38,491
-One more.
-[camera shutter clicks]

43
00:02:40,076 --> 00:02:42,287
Great. Uh, can we get closer, please.

44
00:02:42,370 --> 00:02:43,621
[music stops]

45
00:02:43,705 --> 00:02:46,040
Great, perfect. Uh, look at the camera.

46
00:02:47,208 --> 00:02:48,960
Perfect. Smile.

47
00:02:49,460 --> 00:02:51,713
Let's see that joy for Ale and Arturo.

48
00:02:51,796 --> 00:02:55,133
["Unchained Melody"
by The Righteous Brothers playing]

49
00:02:55,216 --> 00:02:57,135
ALEJANDRA AND ARTURO

50
00:02:57,218 --> 00:02:59,220
OUR WEDDING

51
00:02:59,304 --> 00:03:01,514
[applause and cheering]

52
00:03:02,390 --> 00:03:07,979
♪ <i>I've hungered for your touch ♪</i>

53
00:03:09,564 --> 00:03:14,944
<i>♪ A long, lonely time ♪</i>

54
00:03:17,614 --> 00:03:22,452
[crowd] Kiss! Kiss! Kiss! Kiss! Kiss!

55
00:03:25,079 --> 00:03:28,416
[Alejandra] <i>When I got married,</i>
<i>I think the biggest pressure I felt</i>

56
00:03:28,499 --> 00:03:30,835
<i>was to make his family happy.</i>

57
00:03:30,919 --> 00:03:34,005
<i>I was always really accepted</i>
<i>by my own family,</i>

58
00:03:34,088 --> 00:03:36,633
<i>so being a part of his family</i>

59
00:03:36,716 --> 00:03:39,886
<i>and not feeling accepted by his mother</i>

60
00:03:39,969 --> 00:03:43,556
<i>made me feel like</i>
<i>I had to earn my place </i>to feel accepted.

61
00:03:43,640 --> 00:03:46,851
[all chanting]

62
00:03:46,935 --> 00:03:50,939
Forever together,
always and forever! [cheering]

63
00:03:51,022 --> 00:03:52,023
[machine clicks]

64
00:03:52,106 --> 00:03:53,691
[clock ticking]

65
00:03:54,567 --> 00:03:57,528
[moody dramatic music playing]

66
00:04:11,167 --> 00:04:13,962
[Alejandra] <i>I lost my baby</i>
<i>living with my in-laws.</i>

67
00:04:14,045 --> 00:04:15,797
<i>I didn't want to see anyone.</i>

68
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:19,008
<i>But they came up to my room,</i>
<i>and one of Arturo’s aunts asked me…</i>

69
00:04:19,092 --> 00:04:21,678
-Why are you crying? Don't cry.
<i>-</i>[Alejandra] <i>"Why are you crying?"</i>

70
00:04:21,761 --> 00:04:24,097
<i>-"We've all been there before."</i>
-Yes, it's terrible.

71
00:04:24,180 --> 00:04:26,599
[Alejandra] <i>His mom said,</i>
<i>"It's because you're not careful."</i>

72
00:04:26,683 --> 00:04:27,850
Grandma!

73
00:04:29,018 --> 00:04:30,478
How are you feeling, Ale?

74
00:04:30,561 --> 00:04:34,190
[Alejandra] <i>I had to lie there,</i>
<i>listening to everything they were saying</i>

75
00:04:34,274 --> 00:04:36,150
<i>until my mom got there.</i>

76
00:04:36,859 --> 00:04:38,278
I’m here, honey.

77
00:04:39,445 --> 00:04:40,989
[kissing]

78
00:04:42,615 --> 00:04:44,033
Why did I miscarry?

79
00:04:44,117 --> 00:04:46,244
[moody dramatic music continues]

80
00:04:46,327 --> 00:04:48,788
-[Alejandra<i>] It was my fault.</i>
-It was all my fault.

81
00:04:48,871 --> 00:04:52,542
[Alejandra] <i>Because I didn't take care</i>
<i>of myself. Because I ran, I went to work.</i>

82
00:04:52,625 --> 00:04:56,379
<i>-I blamed myself for everything.</i>
-No, it wasn't your fault, relax.

83
00:04:57,839 --> 00:04:59,507
Get some rest, okay?

84
00:05:01,426 --> 00:05:03,011
[whimpers faintly]

85
00:05:04,762 --> 00:05:06,597
[people chuckle]

86
00:05:07,390 --> 00:05:10,310
Hey, so we're gonna have
a big yard for a party, huh?

87
00:05:10,393 --> 00:05:11,686
-Cheers!
-[people] Cheers.

88
00:05:11,769 --> 00:05:14,397
[woman 1] So the house
is really big then? Congrats.

89
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:16,482
[woman 2] That's super exciting.

90
00:05:16,566 --> 00:05:19,027
-Maybe you'll come over soon.
-[woman 3] Can't wait to see it.

91
00:05:19,110 --> 00:05:21,446
[overlapping chatter]

92
00:05:21,529 --> 00:05:25,408
The house is very nice,
but it's big for them.

93
00:05:25,908 --> 00:05:27,827
-They don't even have children.
-Ma.

94
00:05:27,910 --> 00:05:30,455
-Or maybe they'll fill it with dogs?
-[man 2] Mom, stop.

95
00:05:30,538 --> 00:05:32,248
-Lot of dogs here.
-[man 3] All those rooms,

96
00:05:32,332 --> 00:05:34,917
-you've gotta fill 'em with something.
[man 2] You too, Uncle?

97
00:05:35,001 --> 00:05:37,503
[woman 2] We just want you both
to be happy there.

98
00:05:37,587 --> 00:05:40,506
It would be so nice
to have a few running around there.

99
00:05:40,590 --> 00:05:43,176
[woman 4] I want
to meet a great-grandchild of mine.

100
00:05:43,259 --> 00:05:45,470
Well, yeah, Grandma, but I'm only 25.

101
00:05:45,553 --> 00:05:48,514
Well, you had better
start soon then, dear.

102
00:05:48,598 --> 00:05:51,684
[woman 2] Otherwise, they'll look like
your grandkids instead of your children.

103
00:05:52,435 --> 00:05:53,978
[Arturo's uncle] Why don't you adopt?

104
00:05:54,062 --> 00:05:56,606
No, it's not the same, right?

105
00:05:57,315 --> 00:05:59,317
We're gonna have kids of our own.

106
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:02,820
And Ale has been very busy
working at the hospital, it's demanding.

107
00:06:02,904 --> 00:06:05,656
-But we're on it.
-[Arturo's mother] Those are priorities.

108
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:08,201
-Don't wait too long.
-[Arturo's uncle] Thank you.

109
00:06:08,284 --> 00:06:09,952
-Erik, Another one?
-[Erik] No, thanks.

110
00:06:10,036 --> 00:06:12,080
-Bring me two cold ones, please?
-Yeah.

111
00:06:12,163 --> 00:06:14,749
[quiet ethereal music playing]

112
00:06:14,832 --> 00:06:17,126
[typing]

113
00:06:19,504 --> 00:06:25,051
-[man] What happened after that loss?
-I got pregnant again soon after, right?

114
00:06:25,134 --> 00:06:29,555
Arturo was always telling me, "Careful,
Ale. Don’t do this, don’t do that."

115
00:06:29,639 --> 00:06:32,392
Yeah, we fought the last time
about the pregnancy.

116
00:06:32,475 --> 00:06:34,727
I told her she had to be careful,
had to rest.

117
00:06:34,811 --> 00:06:38,439
I work all day, I can't be following
her around, reminding her.

118
00:06:38,523 --> 00:06:41,401
I even said, "Do it for the baby,
if you can't do it for yourself."

119
00:06:41,484 --> 00:06:43,027
but she's stubborn like that.

120
00:06:43,528 --> 00:06:44,695
I mean it.

121
00:06:46,531 --> 00:06:48,741
And well, I lost that pregnancy.

122
00:06:48,825 --> 00:06:51,369
That was my second time
having a miscarriage.

123
00:06:52,412 --> 00:06:54,997
After a few years
we started to worry, right?

124
00:06:55,081 --> 00:06:57,166
We realized a baby wasn't coming.

125
00:06:58,251 --> 00:07:02,296
Doctor, this is very hard for me, because
I want to have a child and I can't.

126
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:04,090
We don't know what the problem is.

127
00:07:04,173 --> 00:07:07,009
It happened once naturally,
so why won't it happen again?

128
00:07:07,093 --> 00:07:09,387
We're not using any protection, so…

129
00:07:09,470 --> 00:07:13,558
I don't know. I think there's something
wrong in her body that can't keep it like…

130
00:07:14,642 --> 00:07:15,726
I don't know.

131
00:07:16,769 --> 00:07:17,895
[doctor] Don't worry.

132
00:07:17,979 --> 00:07:20,815
We're going to see how your uterus
is doing after the curettage,

133
00:07:20,898 --> 00:07:23,443
and we're also going to analyze
your husband’s semen.

134
00:07:25,319 --> 00:07:27,905
We could even try doing
artificial insemination

135
00:07:27,989 --> 00:07:29,574
to help you get pregnant.

136
00:07:30,158 --> 00:07:31,534
That prevents loses, right?

137
00:07:31,617 --> 00:07:34,495
No pregnancy is guaranteed
to succeed 100%.

138
00:07:36,205 --> 00:07:40,626
But nature is wise, and it won’t allow
an unhealthy baby to reach full term.

139
00:07:41,878 --> 00:07:44,922
You are both very young.
You still have time.

140
00:07:45,006 --> 00:07:46,757
[exhales deeply]

141
00:07:48,092 --> 00:07:50,678
[Alejandra's mother] Okay, okay, okay,
almost there, almost there.

142
00:07:52,597 --> 00:07:54,140
You'll be all right.

143
00:07:54,765 --> 00:07:56,058
Thanks.

144
00:07:59,061 --> 00:08:02,064
[moody dramatic music playing]

145
00:08:09,238 --> 00:08:11,949
[whimsical ethereal music playing]

146
00:08:12,033 --> 00:08:15,495
[Alejandra] <i>When I finally got pregnant</i>
<i>the third time, Arturo said,</i>

147
00:08:15,578 --> 00:08:17,413
<i>"Now you have to take care of yourself."</i>

148
00:08:17,497 --> 00:08:20,249
<i>"Now you have to do this,</i>
now <i>you have to do that."</i>

149
00:08:20,333 --> 00:08:22,168
<i>"Now you need to stay here.</i>"

150
00:08:22,251 --> 00:08:25,046
<i>"Actually, you have to stop working."</i>

151
00:08:25,129 --> 00:08:29,592
<i>And I was like, "No, what are you talking</i>
<i>about? I'm not going to stop working."</i>

152
00:08:29,675 --> 00:08:31,844
<i>And he would say, "You are so stubborn."</i>

153
00:08:31,928 --> 00:08:33,888
-Hi, Ale.
-Hi, doctor.

154
00:08:33,971 --> 00:08:35,223
How are you feeling?

155
00:08:35,306 --> 00:08:37,642
Great. I'm not nauseous anymore.

156
00:08:37,725 --> 00:08:39,852
-Is everything ready?
-Uh-huh.

157
00:08:39,936 --> 00:08:41,938
Hello. Good morning. Come in.

158
00:08:44,065 --> 00:08:46,442
-Thank you. We'll have coffee now, okay?
-Okay.

159
00:08:58,079 --> 00:09:00,581
[moody music playing]

160
00:09:13,302 --> 00:09:15,638
[Alejandra] <i>I showed up</i>
<i>at my boss's office crying</i>

161
00:09:15,721 --> 00:09:17,265
<i>and said, "I don't feel well."</i>

162
00:09:17,348 --> 00:09:22,478
Ale, I'm so sorry,
but with the bleeding… the baby's gone.

163
00:09:23,354 --> 00:09:25,064
Oh no, not again.

164
00:09:26,148 --> 00:09:27,400
I'm sorry.

165
00:09:29,193 --> 00:09:31,195
How am I going to tell Arturo, doctor?

166
00:09:31,279 --> 00:09:32,780
Try to relax, hm?

167
00:09:33,322 --> 00:09:34,699
Relax and

168
00:09:35,408 --> 00:09:38,035
talk to your husband,
discuss your options.

169
00:09:38,119 --> 00:09:42,206
It's going to be very difficult for you
to have a pregnancy reach full-term.

170
00:09:44,917 --> 00:09:46,544
I'll let you get dressed.

171
00:10:17,450 --> 00:10:21,412
[Alejandra] <i>Afterwards,</i>
<i>I sat in the clinic waiting room</i>

172
00:10:21,495 --> 00:10:23,706
<i>with mixed feelings.</i>

173
00:10:23,789 --> 00:10:26,042
<i>I blamed myself, obviously.</i>

174
00:10:26,125 --> 00:10:27,668
[moody music stops]

175
00:10:29,378 --> 00:10:32,506
Look, can someone please help me?
I've been waiting here for hours.

176
00:10:32,590 --> 00:10:34,550
[receptionist] You have to wait your turn.

177
00:10:34,634 --> 00:10:35,843
You can't do anything?

178
00:10:35,926 --> 00:10:37,720
[Alejandra] <i>You ask God, "Why me?"</i>

179
00:10:37,803 --> 00:10:40,806
<i>"Why is this happening? Why?"</i>

180
00:10:41,307 --> 00:10:43,434
<i>That’s when I met Mayra.</i>

181
00:10:43,517 --> 00:10:45,770
[whimpering quietly]

182
00:10:50,024 --> 00:10:51,400
What's wrong?

183
00:10:55,529 --> 00:10:57,365
I want to be a mom, and I can’t.

184
00:10:59,575 --> 00:11:01,410
I'm going to be a mom, and don't want to.

185
00:11:01,494 --> 00:11:03,746
[quiet dramatic music playing]

186
00:11:04,246 --> 00:11:05,289
What?

187
00:11:06,332 --> 00:11:07,333
I just found out.

188
00:11:07,416 --> 00:11:08,751
[Alejandra] <i>Mayra tells me…</i>

189
00:11:08,834 --> 00:11:11,462
-I don't want to have it.
-[Alejandra] <i>…she wanted an abortion.</i>

190
00:11:12,755 --> 00:11:14,882
<i>The dad doesn't want</i>
<i>to take responsibility</i>

191
00:11:14,965 --> 00:11:16,592
<i>because he says it's not his.</i>

192
00:11:16,676 --> 00:11:19,261
And I… I can’t have another baby.

193
00:11:23,099 --> 00:11:25,518
But, but you can have it by yourself.

194
00:11:25,601 --> 00:11:26,602
No.

195
00:11:26,686 --> 00:11:28,312
I don't study or work.

196
00:11:28,813 --> 00:11:30,773
I just help my mom with stuff.

197
00:11:31,774 --> 00:11:33,609
[actress] You can get a job.

198
00:11:33,693 --> 00:11:35,194
Sell something, I don't know.

199
00:11:35,277 --> 00:11:37,947
No, no, no, working isn't for me.

200
00:11:38,030 --> 00:11:40,366
I do sell some stuff, but no.

201
00:11:41,158 --> 00:11:43,869
No. I can’t have another baby.

202
00:11:44,745 --> 00:11:48,541
I already have a daughter. If I have
another baby, my mom will kill me.

203
00:11:48,624 --> 00:11:50,876
She'll kick me out of the house
and go crazy.

204
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:53,087
She wouldn't be able to kick you out.

205
00:11:53,170 --> 00:11:54,588
Yeah, she will.

206
00:11:59,093 --> 00:12:00,302
Oh, man.

207
00:12:01,679 --> 00:12:03,764
I'd rather give it away
than get rid of it.

208
00:12:04,974 --> 00:12:05,975
I guess.

209
00:12:07,017 --> 00:12:10,354
[Alejandra] <i>Then, she says, "I'd rather</i>
<i>give it away than get rid of it."</i>

210
00:12:10,438 --> 00:12:11,522
What?

211
00:12:15,484 --> 00:12:17,111
I wanna give it away.

212
00:12:17,653 --> 00:12:19,905
[gentle upbeat music playing]

213
00:12:24,452 --> 00:12:25,870
Are you serious?

214
00:12:28,748 --> 00:12:29,749
Yes.

215
00:12:32,418 --> 00:12:36,505
[Alejandra] <i>And at the time,</i>
<i>you think it's God,</i>

216
00:12:36,589 --> 00:12:38,758
<i>fate, the universe…</i>

217
00:12:38,841 --> 00:12:41,177
If you’re sure, I can keep your baby.

218
00:12:41,260 --> 00:12:43,137
[Alejandra] <i>…that puts people</i>
<i>in your path,</i>

219
00:12:43,220 --> 00:12:45,431
<i>and maybe God wants you</i>
<i>to do something, right?</i>

220
00:12:45,514 --> 00:12:46,599
[Mayra] Yes.

221
00:12:46,682 --> 00:12:49,560
I swear, I'll take care
of everything for your baby.

222
00:12:51,312 --> 00:12:52,688
I promise you.

223
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:55,775
My name's Mayra.

224
00:12:59,028 --> 00:13:01,113
[actress]
Nice to meet you. I'm Ale.

225
00:13:01,989 --> 00:13:03,199
[sighs]

226
00:13:03,991 --> 00:13:05,075
Look.

227
00:13:06,035 --> 00:13:07,036
{\an8}OBGYN ADMIN SUPPORT

228
00:13:07,119 --> 00:13:08,579
{\an8}I work in Gynecology.

229
00:13:08,662 --> 00:13:10,164
Yes, I noticed.

230
00:13:12,291 --> 00:13:15,878
I guess we can start your paperwork
so you can have your appointments here.

231
00:13:15,961 --> 00:13:16,837
Okay.

232
00:13:16,921 --> 00:13:19,089
PERSONAL INFORMATION

233
00:13:19,173 --> 00:13:22,551
[Alejandra] <i>Deep down, I was worried</i>
<i>that she would try to blackmail me,</i>

234
00:13:22,635 --> 00:13:25,262
<i>so the less information</i>
<i>she had about me, the better.</i>

235
00:13:25,888 --> 00:13:29,892
<i>So I said, "I'll see you here.</i>
<i>I work in Women's Health."</i>

236
00:13:29,975 --> 00:13:33,229
<i>"Don't worry.</i>
<i>Whatever you need, I'll be here."</i>

237
00:13:33,312 --> 00:13:35,773
This lets you have
all your appointments here.

238
00:13:36,357 --> 00:13:39,276
And I also made
your ultrasound appointment.

239
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:41,737
-We'll see you April 20th.
-Yeah.

240
00:13:42,530 --> 00:13:44,114
-At eight.
-Mm-hm.

241
00:13:46,367 --> 00:13:48,661
[mysterious music playing]

242
00:13:59,338 --> 00:14:01,423
[moody dramatic music playing]

243
00:14:03,133 --> 00:14:05,970
[Alejandra] <i>I went home,</i>
<i>and when I got there I thought,</i>

244
00:14:06,053 --> 00:14:07,847
<i>"I'm not gonna tell anyone."</i>

245
00:14:09,807 --> 00:14:11,809
<i>Mostly, I wasn't telling Arturo.</i>

246
00:14:13,185 --> 00:14:16,689
<i>Why? Because I didn’t want to be blamed.</i>

247
00:14:17,314 --> 00:14:19,859
<i>I didn't want to hear,</i>
<i>yet again, "I told you so,"</i>

248
00:14:19,942 --> 00:14:23,070
<i>or "It's your fault,"</i>
<i>or, "You don't understand."</i>

249
00:14:37,626 --> 00:14:40,296
[moody dramatic music fades]

250
00:14:40,379 --> 00:14:43,257
4 MONTHS PREGNANT: YOUR BODY TRANSFORMS

251
00:14:43,340 --> 00:14:44,884
PHYSICAL AND HORMONAL CHANGES

252
00:14:44,967 --> 00:14:47,052
[whispering] Shut the baby…

253
00:14:48,178 --> 00:14:50,681
[lively classical music playing]

254
00:14:52,182 --> 00:14:53,976
THE POWER OF PREGNANCY

255
00:14:54,059 --> 00:14:58,230
FOODS THAT CAUSE WEIGHT GAIN

256
00:15:09,199 --> 00:15:10,826
[music stops]

257
00:15:10,910 --> 00:15:12,995
-You say no. Doesn't make sense.
-What's the problem?

258
00:15:13,078 --> 00:15:15,497
What were you doing? We couldn't find you.

259
00:15:15,581 --> 00:15:17,374
-I was at school.
-He says he was at school.

260
00:15:17,458 --> 00:15:19,293
-That's what he says.
-Here you are.

261
00:15:19,376 --> 00:15:20,753
Mom always has my back.

262
00:15:20,836 --> 00:15:23,047
[Arturo’s mother]
This pozole looks really good.

263
00:15:23,130 --> 00:15:25,132
Hey, damn, I want what you're having.

264
00:15:25,215 --> 00:15:28,677
Well, this is my pregnant diet
by my doctor, okay?

265
00:15:28,761 --> 00:15:30,971
[Erik] Well, introduce me
to that doctor, please.

266
00:15:31,055 --> 00:15:34,058
-Hey, respect my wife. Mom, look at him.
-[Erik chuckles]

267
00:15:34,767 --> 00:15:37,436
-[Arturo's mother] How are you feeling?
-Fine.

268
00:15:37,519 --> 00:15:40,773
[Arturo's mother] You can't tell from
your eyes. Her eyes don't look sunken.

269
00:15:40,856 --> 00:15:43,609
-[Arturo] Mom, stop.
-I think that's an old wives' tales.

270
00:15:43,692 --> 00:15:45,402
Stop. Hey.

271
00:15:45,486 --> 00:15:49,365
Hey, sweetie,
I bought you some ground beef. Come here.

272
00:15:49,448 --> 00:15:52,534
Peppers, to make stuffed peppers
and some eggs.

273
00:15:52,618 --> 00:15:55,537
-And people say I don't spoil him.
-[Erik] Oh, yeah.

274
00:15:55,621 --> 00:15:58,749
Would you look,
I even iron his clothes, and I'm pregnant.

275
00:15:58,832 --> 00:16:02,252
Well, pregnancy isn't a malady,
my dear. You can do anything.

276
00:16:02,336 --> 00:16:04,004
No, Mom, she can't do anything.

277
00:16:04,588 --> 00:16:07,257
She's already had two miscarriages.
She has to be careful.

278
00:16:07,341 --> 00:16:09,885
[Arturo's mother]
Well, I'm from a different time.

279
00:16:10,844 --> 00:16:12,721
[Arturo] You okay? What’s wrong?

280
00:16:14,515 --> 00:16:17,184
She's still having a lot of nausea
from the pregnancy.

281
00:16:17,267 --> 00:16:18,519
She'll be right back.

282
00:16:18,602 --> 00:16:21,313
-Do you like it? Not eating much.
-[Arturo's mother] Mm-hm.

283
00:16:21,397 --> 00:16:23,440
[mysterious music playing]

284
00:16:27,987 --> 00:16:30,990
[Alejandra] <i>So far,</i>
<i>everything was going as planned.</i>

285
00:16:31,490 --> 00:16:33,242
<i>Arturo believed me.</i>

286
00:16:33,742 --> 00:16:36,328
<i>He really thought that I was pregnant.</i>

287
00:16:38,956 --> 00:16:41,583
-How far along are you?
-Five months.

288
00:16:41,667 --> 00:16:44,420
Ale, why did you change jobs?

289
00:16:44,503 --> 00:16:47,131
Yeah, I mean,
Urology is much more demanding.

290
00:16:47,798 --> 00:16:51,260
Besides, all pregnant women are treated
in Gynecology with Dr. Guerrero.

291
00:16:51,343 --> 00:16:55,180
-It’s easier if you're working there.
-No, I've been needing a new job.

292
00:16:55,264 --> 00:16:57,182
Gynecology is too much.

293
00:16:57,266 --> 00:16:59,601
[nurse 1] But, Ale,
you're five months pregnant.

294
00:16:59,685 --> 00:17:03,814
You should have stayed there
doing paperwork, sitting at your desk.

295
00:17:04,732 --> 00:17:07,317
No, it seems like normal hours,
eight to three,

296
00:17:07,401 --> 00:17:10,029
but no, you always have to do extra.

297
00:17:10,112 --> 00:17:11,238
[nurse 2] Hm.

298
00:17:11,321 --> 00:17:13,949
Every night,
it was really stressful for me to stay.

299
00:17:14,033 --> 00:17:16,785
All the time, Arturo keeps saying,
"Hey, Alejandra,

300
00:17:16,869 --> 00:17:18,787
you can't keep doing this."

301
00:17:18,871 --> 00:17:20,664
"You get home so late."

302
00:17:20,748 --> 00:17:23,459
[nurse 2] Yeah, I get it.
A man need his wife, right?

303
00:17:23,542 --> 00:17:24,668
[chuckles]

304
00:17:24,752 --> 00:17:28,130
[nurse 1] Well, my sister's husband
left her basically overnight

305
00:17:28,213 --> 00:17:29,715
for far less than that.

306
00:17:29,798 --> 00:17:32,676
-Oh my God, heaven forbid.
-[nurse 2] Are you serious? No.

307
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:35,012
Imagine him leaving now.

308
00:17:35,095 --> 00:17:36,430
[nurse 2 chuckles]

309
00:17:36,513 --> 00:17:37,806
No, no, no.

310
00:17:37,890 --> 00:17:40,184
No. But that's why I behave.

311
00:17:40,267 --> 00:17:42,561
I mean, we're happier like this.

312
00:17:42,644 --> 00:17:44,396
[nurse 2 chuckles]

313
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:47,316
Well, I hope it's what's best
for you three of you.

314
00:17:47,399 --> 00:17:49,401
-Do you want some water?
-Yes, please.

315
00:17:49,485 --> 00:17:51,945
[quiet ethereal music playing]

316
00:17:56,366 --> 00:17:59,620
THE POWER OF PREGNANCY

317
00:18:00,412 --> 00:18:04,041
[Alejandra] <i>When I started gaining weight,</i>
<i>everything began to change.</i>

318
00:18:04,124 --> 00:18:08,337
<i>Absolutely everything, my body,</i>
<i>having to buy maternity clothes.</i>

319
00:18:10,589 --> 00:18:12,216
<i>With all the weight I was gaining,</i>

320
00:18:12,299 --> 00:18:15,552
<i>my stomach really looked</i>
<i>like a pregnancy bump,</i>

321
00:18:15,636 --> 00:18:19,014
<i>So, when Arturo and I were intimate,</i>

322
00:18:19,098 --> 00:18:23,352
<i>whenever I felt his hand on my stomach,</i>
<i>I instinctively tightened my muscles</i>

323
00:18:23,435 --> 00:18:24,895
<i>so it felt more firm.</i>

324
00:18:24,978 --> 00:18:27,606
Arturo. Arturo. Arturo, no.

325
00:18:27,689 --> 00:18:29,441
-I know, but I want to.
-I can’t.

326
00:18:29,525 --> 00:18:32,611
-The doctor told me not right now.
-But why not? Come on.

327
00:18:32,694 --> 00:18:35,155
-I can't do it. I can't do this right now.
-Why?

328
00:18:35,239 --> 00:18:37,491
-I'm telling you, no.
-[sighs]

329
00:18:37,574 --> 00:18:39,076
It can be dangerous.

330
00:18:40,577 --> 00:18:43,580
-It could cause a premature baby birth.
-[sighs]

331
00:18:44,081 --> 00:18:46,625
What if we hit its head
and he comes early?

332
00:18:48,043 --> 00:18:50,379
He said it was called something like

333
00:18:50,462 --> 00:18:53,632
total occlusion placenta previa.

334
00:18:55,801 --> 00:18:57,803
Your stomach is hard but it looks small.

335
00:18:57,886 --> 00:19:00,931
The baby's small
and that's the problem, you know?

336
00:19:02,516 --> 00:19:05,227
When are you having
another checkup at the hospital?

337
00:19:05,727 --> 00:19:07,104
I don't know.

338
00:19:07,187 --> 00:19:10,023
The other day,
your mom wanted to see an ultrasound.

339
00:19:10,107 --> 00:19:12,401
They already did it
and everything was good.

340
00:19:12,901 --> 00:19:17,114
And the others, the other ultrasounds,
when did you do them?

341
00:19:17,197 --> 00:19:20,284
About a month ago.
I don't have the copies yet.

342
00:19:20,367 --> 00:19:22,161
I mean, Arturo,

343
00:19:22,244 --> 00:19:25,914
I do all of it at the hospital,
but I didn't get anything.

344
00:19:26,415 --> 00:19:29,877
Mm. And nowhere else
is going to do better.

345
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:31,003
Yeah?

346
00:19:31,086 --> 00:19:32,546
Well, all right then.

347
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:38,385
If you're happy, I'm happy.

348
00:19:38,927 --> 00:19:41,597
[Alejandra] <i>I slept next to him,</i>
<i>I had lived with him.</i>

349
00:19:41,680 --> 00:19:44,474
<i>If he said something, I’d immediately say,</i>

350
00:19:44,558 --> 00:19:46,226
<i>"You're bothering me."</i>

351
00:19:46,727 --> 00:19:48,770
<i>-"You’re hurting me."</i>
-[Arturo sighs]

352
00:19:48,854 --> 00:19:50,814
<i>"Don't you know that hurts?"</i>

353
00:19:51,565 --> 00:19:55,444
<i>I guess it was the same kind of emotional</i>
<i>blackmail I always used on him.</i>

354
00:19:56,737 --> 00:19:58,572
-How are you?
-Fine

355
00:20:03,285 --> 00:20:06,079
Hmm. Did you get the ultrasound?

356
00:20:06,163 --> 00:20:09,958
Yes, but they had me waiting for hours.
Haven't eaten anything.

357
00:20:10,876 --> 00:20:11,960
Let's see.

358
00:20:15,214 --> 00:20:16,506
Have some.

359
00:20:19,718 --> 00:20:21,762
I also brought your vitamins.

360
00:20:23,305 --> 00:20:24,681
Take them, okay?

361
00:20:25,182 --> 00:20:26,934
Did they say anything?

362
00:20:28,602 --> 00:20:31,480
It's a girl, and she's underweight.

363
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:36,568
Hey, you're getting fat.

364
00:20:37,236 --> 00:20:39,071
Are you sure you're not pregnant?

365
00:20:39,154 --> 00:20:41,615
Oh no, I wish. Mmm.

366
00:20:41,698 --> 00:20:43,200
What do you mean?

367
00:20:48,664 --> 00:20:50,332
Is there a due date?

368
00:20:50,415 --> 00:20:51,541
[Mayra] Mm-hm.

369
00:20:53,335 --> 00:20:55,963
They think I'll give birth
the week of June 16th.

370
00:20:58,715 --> 00:21:01,426
I have to go. I've been here all morning.

371
00:21:01,510 --> 00:21:02,594
[zipper zips]

372
00:21:03,303 --> 00:21:04,346
Okay.

373
00:21:09,309 --> 00:21:12,187
You're not alone. I'm always here. Hm?

374
00:21:13,313 --> 00:21:14,481
[kiss]

375
00:21:16,858 --> 00:21:19,319
-See you in two months.
-Yeah.

376
00:21:20,070 --> 00:21:21,863
I'll see you on June 16th.

377
00:21:28,787 --> 00:21:29,955
ULTRASOUND

378
00:21:30,038 --> 00:21:32,708
[quiet ethereal music playing]

379
00:21:32,791 --> 00:21:35,252
[typing]

380
00:21:45,887 --> 00:21:48,598
[actress] Let me introduce
our new family member.

381
00:21:48,682 --> 00:21:50,142
They finally gave it to you?

382
00:21:50,225 --> 00:21:53,603
See, my love? That's the advantage
of not leaving the hospital.

383
00:21:54,521 --> 00:21:57,024
You both have no idea
how hard it was to get them.

384
00:21:57,107 --> 00:22:00,319
-I explained that it was important to me.
-How are you, little guy.

385
00:22:00,402 --> 00:22:02,738
Hello, baby Arturo.
He's Arturo junior, yeah?

386
00:22:02,821 --> 00:22:04,531
-Why does that matter?
-What do you mean?

387
00:22:04,614 --> 00:22:06,366
Because maybe it's a girl!

388
00:22:06,450 --> 00:22:09,161
It doesn't look like a girl
from how you're carrying.

389
00:22:09,244 --> 00:22:11,705
-That's what the doctors said.
-You're not a girl.

390
00:22:11,788 --> 00:22:13,957
Don't worry, Arturo, it's not a girl.

391
00:22:14,041 --> 00:22:16,668
-I think that they'd know. [chuckles]
-You hear that?

392
00:22:16,752 --> 00:22:20,047
-Either way, it'll be God's will. Right?
-Yeah. It's God's will.

393
00:22:20,130 --> 00:22:22,257
-Yeah.
-Daddy loves you, little Arturo.

394
00:22:22,341 --> 00:22:24,426
-Need anything?
-[actress] Yes.

395
00:22:24,509 --> 00:22:25,844
Tea, please.

396
00:22:28,138 --> 00:22:31,391
"They're going to have a house full
of dogs. I won't get to have grandkids."

397
00:22:31,475 --> 00:22:33,477
I'll fill the house
with dogs that bite you,

398
00:22:33,560 --> 00:22:36,646
-dumb mother-in-law. [groans]
-Hey. Go easy, that's my mother.

399
00:22:36,730 --> 00:22:39,066
She loves you very much.
She asks about you.

400
00:22:39,149 --> 00:22:41,443
She's very happy that you're pregnant.

401
00:22:41,526 --> 00:22:43,403
-Yeah, I can tell.
-[scoffs]

402
00:22:43,487 --> 00:22:45,655
Look at this one. It's so cute.

403
00:22:45,739 --> 00:22:46,948
Yeah, it's cute.

404
00:22:47,574 --> 00:22:51,828
I think maybe one that's a little longer,
yeah, at the bottom?

405
00:22:53,497 --> 00:22:54,539
My love.

406
00:22:55,540 --> 00:22:57,918
One of my friends bought this
for her baby.

407
00:22:58,835 --> 00:23:00,087
She's adopting him.

408
00:23:00,170 --> 00:23:03,048
Yeah, her mom didn't want him
and can't take care of him.

409
00:23:03,131 --> 00:23:05,133
So, well, she's going to keep him.

410
00:23:07,052 --> 00:23:09,805
-Arturo, I’m talking to you.
-So, I’m listening.

411
00:23:09,888 --> 00:23:11,681
You're not paying attention though.

412
00:23:11,765 --> 00:23:13,892
What do you want me to say? "It's fine"?

413
00:23:13,975 --> 00:23:16,770
She should try her best,
even if the kid isn't hers.

414
00:23:16,853 --> 00:23:19,856
But the kid is hers, yeah?
If she raises it, it's hers.

415
00:23:20,857 --> 00:23:22,526
Yeah, but it's not the same.

416
00:23:22,609 --> 00:23:24,194
I could never adopt a baby.

417
00:23:24,861 --> 00:23:26,988
-Okay, but why?
-Just because.

418
00:23:27,489 --> 00:23:30,367
It's not the same.
I don't want to hurt the kid, you know?

419
00:23:30,867 --> 00:23:32,869
What if I can't love him like I should?

420
00:23:35,539 --> 00:23:37,082
[groans] Ale.

421
00:23:39,084 --> 00:23:40,669
-Why are you getting upset?
-Mm.

422
00:23:40,752 --> 00:23:42,879
Calm down. Don't let the baby hear.

423
00:23:43,463 --> 00:23:45,257
If it’s a boy, he'll look like you.

424
00:23:45,340 --> 00:23:47,843
If it’s a girl, she'll look like me.

425
00:23:48,343 --> 00:23:50,846
Mm. As long as my girl's
not like your mom, all right?

426
00:23:50,929 --> 00:23:52,806
Hey, that's my mom.

427
00:23:55,767 --> 00:23:57,769
[ethereal music playing]

428
00:24:03,066 --> 00:24:04,734
[Alejandra] <i>I felt very special.</i>

429
00:24:05,402 --> 00:24:07,404
<i>From the minute the people who love you</i>

430
00:24:07,487 --> 00:24:10,449
<i>start treating you</i>
<i>with that kind of affection,</i>

431
00:24:11,158 --> 00:24:14,870
<i>filled with anticipation</i>
<i>and with, with hope,</i>

432
00:24:14,953 --> 00:24:17,080
where they see you and touch your belly

433
00:24:17,164 --> 00:24:19,708
<i>and, and they treat you so nicely…</i>

434
00:24:19,791 --> 00:24:22,085
-Everything's so pretty.
-Thank you.

435
00:24:22,169 --> 00:24:24,963
-You look pretty too, Ale.
-[laughter]

436
00:24:25,547 --> 00:24:26,923
Okay, that one's done.

437
00:24:28,300 --> 00:24:30,719
So exciting! Are you excited?

438
00:24:30,802 --> 00:24:31,928
Oh, yeah.

439
00:24:32,721 --> 00:24:34,681
[woman 1] The prettiest aunt around.

440
00:24:34,764 --> 00:24:36,558
Look at that. Here I am.

441
00:24:36,641 --> 00:24:38,518
[woman 1] What would you name the baby?

442
00:24:38,602 --> 00:24:39,853
NAME OPTIONS

443
00:24:39,936 --> 00:24:43,190
{\an8}-If it's a girl, Alejandra.
-[woman 1] Uh-huh. Okay.

444
00:24:45,442 --> 00:24:47,986
{\an8}If it’s a boy,
I’d like him to be called Arturo.

445
00:24:48,069 --> 00:24:51,031
{\an8}-[woman 1] There already two Arturos.
-After their dad and mom.

446
00:24:51,114 --> 00:24:53,992
{\an8}-Aww, look how pretty.
-[woman 1 laughs]

447
00:24:54,075 --> 00:24:57,329
-Yes, there's that and here are the girls.
-[woman 2] "Alejandra's baby shower."

448
00:24:57,412 --> 00:24:59,206
-[woman 1] Say hi!
-[woman 3] Mom of the year.

449
00:24:59,289 --> 00:25:01,416
[woman 1] We love it. What do we say?

450
00:25:01,500 --> 00:25:02,792
Let's do this!

451
00:25:02,876 --> 00:25:06,505
[women] Mom of the year!
Mom of the year!

452
00:25:06,588 --> 00:25:09,341
Mom of the year! Mom of the year!

453
00:25:09,424 --> 00:25:11,301
[woman 1] Ale, smile!

454
00:25:11,384 --> 00:25:15,138
All right, it’s okay. What are we missing?
Let’s see. Anything else?

455
00:25:16,181 --> 00:25:19,059
Let's all clap for the baby!

456
00:25:19,142 --> 00:25:22,979
Give me an A, an L and an E!
Give me an A, an L and an E!

457
00:25:23,063 --> 00:25:26,525
Put it all together now
and what does that spell?

458
00:25:26,608 --> 00:25:30,320
Ale! Ale! Rah! Rah! Rah!

459
00:25:30,403 --> 00:25:31,530
[woman] Congratulations!

460
00:25:31,613 --> 00:25:34,824
[entertainer] You have only one month left
before your baby's born.

461
00:25:34,908 --> 00:25:38,036
Do you have anything
you want to say to your guests?

462
00:25:38,119 --> 00:25:43,124
-[women] Ale! Ale! Ale! Ale! Ale!
-Yes. Boy. Well…

463
00:25:43,208 --> 00:25:47,254
[Alejandra] <i>I feel like I was living</i>
<i>in, in another dimension. I don’t know.</i>

464
00:25:47,337 --> 00:25:49,089
Well, uh, um…

465
00:25:49,172 --> 00:25:53,051
Firstly, I want to thank you all
for being here.

466
00:25:54,844 --> 00:25:56,137
And, um, I

467
00:25:57,138 --> 00:25:58,640
just wanna say…

468
00:25:58,723 --> 00:26:00,433
[shuddering]

469
00:26:00,517 --> 00:26:03,395
-…I couldn't be… uh, uh…
-[quiet dramatic music playing]

470
00:26:03,478 --> 00:26:04,771
…more grateful, yeah,

471
00:26:05,564 --> 00:26:07,440
having you here celebrating with me.

472
00:26:07,524 --> 00:26:09,985
[Alejandra] <i>There were so any times</i>
<i>I just wanted to say,</i>

473
00:26:10,068 --> 00:26:13,238
<i>"It's not real.</i>
<i>This isn't happening." But I couldn't.</i>

474
00:26:13,321 --> 00:26:17,033
-[entertainer] Anyone else? The grandmas?
-Me! Me! I want to say something.

475
00:26:17,534 --> 00:26:19,244
I mean, I just…

476
00:26:20,287 --> 00:26:22,038
I want to thank you all

477
00:26:22,122 --> 00:26:24,916
for coming to celebrate with me and Ale.

478
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:30,380
Because this baby has been
long-awaited by this family.

479
00:26:30,880 --> 00:26:33,508
I hope everything goes well, my dear.

480
00:26:34,301 --> 00:26:35,885
This baby will be cute.

481
00:26:36,428 --> 00:26:38,513
-Hmm?
-[women] Bravo!

482
00:26:38,597 --> 00:26:42,017
Okay, everybody, let's eat.
Come on, there's so much to eat.

483
00:26:42,100 --> 00:26:43,602
Come on. Let me serve you.

484
00:26:43,685 --> 00:26:45,437
[Alejandra] <i>I was really suffering.</i>

485
00:26:45,520 --> 00:26:48,023
<i>I mean, I pretended like I was fine,</i>

486
00:26:48,106 --> 00:26:51,443
<i>but I was suffering on the inside.</i>

487
00:26:51,526 --> 00:26:55,196
<i>I mean, it hurt to see</i>
<i>how happy my parents were,</i>

488
00:26:55,280 --> 00:26:57,741
<i>my family, my grandmother.</i>

489
00:26:57,824 --> 00:27:00,285
[no audible dialogue]

490
00:27:00,910 --> 00:27:04,122
<i>I wish someone</i>
<i>had burst that bubble of lies</i>

491
00:27:04,205 --> 00:27:06,458
<i>and made everything come out.</i>

492
00:27:07,292 --> 00:27:11,004
<i>I wish right there and then</i>
<i>someone would've said, "Wake up!"</i>

493
00:27:19,095 --> 00:27:21,598
[quiet dramatic music fades]

494
00:27:22,223 --> 00:27:24,351
-[Alejandra's mother] Like that one?
-[actress] Yes.

495
00:27:24,434 --> 00:27:27,103
-That's with the discount, right?
-Yes, 20% off.

496
00:27:27,187 --> 00:27:28,772
Arturo, this one.

497
00:27:29,356 --> 00:27:31,691
Did you see this one? It’s the same.

498
00:27:31,775 --> 00:27:33,652
It's not the same. I like this one.

499
00:27:33,735 --> 00:27:37,656
[Arturo] Aren't you getting ahead of
yourself with color? What if it's a boy?

500
00:27:37,739 --> 00:27:40,033
Well, do you have to like it,
or maybe it's me.

501
00:27:40,784 --> 00:27:42,869
-[Arturo] Mm.
-[actress] I like this one.

502
00:27:43,578 --> 00:27:44,913
All right, it's fine.

503
00:27:45,580 --> 00:27:47,624
We’ll take this one, pretty please.

504
00:27:47,707 --> 00:27:48,750
Thanks.

505
00:27:50,502 --> 00:27:51,836
I want to sit down.

506
00:27:53,421 --> 00:27:58,176
[Alejandra] <i>I was so, so fat.</i>
<i>I mean, literally weighed 98 kilos.</i>

507
00:27:58,259 --> 00:28:00,929
<i>I had gained way too much weight.</i>

508
00:28:01,012 --> 00:28:02,847
<i>I didn't feel good. Everything hurt.</i>

509
00:28:02,931 --> 00:28:04,766
I get tired when I stand up too long.

510
00:28:04,849 --> 00:28:07,644
[Alejandra] <i>And Arturo was thinking,</i>
<i>"Something's not right."</i>

511
00:28:07,727 --> 00:28:10,146
-It's okay, my love.
-[Alejandra] <i>"Something’s wrong."</i>

512
00:28:10,230 --> 00:28:13,650
-Time for maternity leave.
-No, I won't stop, I can't stop.

513
00:28:13,733 --> 00:28:16,027
You know me, I can keep working there, so…

514
00:28:16,111 --> 00:28:19,280
Ale, why won't you just go on leave?

515
00:28:19,781 --> 00:28:21,324
It's good for the baby.

516
00:28:22,117 --> 00:28:24,703
Okay, yeah, you're right, okay.

517
00:28:24,786 --> 00:28:27,205
-But just leave me alone.
-I’ll go with you, okay?

518
00:28:27,747 --> 00:28:30,125
No, Arturo, you don't have to go with me.

519
00:28:30,917 --> 00:28:33,044
No way. You're taking me.

520
00:28:33,128 --> 00:28:35,422
-It's not necessary.
-You're taking me with you.

521
00:28:35,505 --> 00:28:39,759
{\an8}LAB ORDER - PATIENT NAME:
MARÍN MENDOZA, ELEONOR ALEJANDRA

522
00:28:42,762 --> 00:28:44,806
[Alejandra] <i>I couldn't keep</i>
<i>excluding Arturo.</i>

523
00:28:44,889 --> 00:28:46,933
<i>Since I worked for so long</i>
<i>at the hospital,</i>

524
00:28:47,016 --> 00:28:49,269
<i>well, I learned how to do a few things</i>

525
00:28:49,352 --> 00:28:52,188
<i>and had some clinical knowledge.</i>

526
00:28:52,272 --> 00:28:54,566
<i>So, I created my own medical records.</i>

527
00:28:54,649 --> 00:28:55,775
MEDICAL RECORD

528
00:28:55,859 --> 00:28:59,404
{\an8}12 WEEKS - 14 WEEKS - 17 WEEKS

529
00:28:59,487 --> 00:29:02,532
{\an8}20 WEEKS - 22 WEEKS - 27 WEEKS

530
00:29:02,615 --> 00:29:05,243
[intriguing music playing]

531
00:29:08,204 --> 00:29:10,832
<i>When we went</i>
<i>to request my maternity leave,</i>

532
00:29:10,915 --> 00:29:13,752
<i>I was thinking,</i>
<i>"How do I get out of here?"</i>

533
00:29:13,835 --> 00:29:17,505
<i>"What's my escape route</i>
<i>when they find out that I'm not pregnant?"</i>

534
00:29:17,589 --> 00:29:20,633
<i>-"They’ll say I'm crazy, insane."</i>
-[doctor] How far along are you?

535
00:29:23,011 --> 00:29:24,179
Uh, ma'am?

536
00:29:24,679 --> 00:29:26,556
How far along are you?

537
00:29:27,807 --> 00:29:29,517
Uh, 38 weeks, so--

538
00:29:29,601 --> 00:29:32,103
[doctor] Good. And how do you feel?

539
00:29:32,854 --> 00:29:33,897
Fine.

540
00:29:34,564 --> 00:29:38,568
[doctor] Any pain, dizziness,
nausea? Trouble sleeping?

541
00:29:39,360 --> 00:29:40,570
No, nothing.

542
00:29:40,653 --> 00:29:44,324
[doctor] Good. I'm going to place a device
to listen to the baby’s heartbeat.

543
00:29:44,407 --> 00:29:45,450
Okay?

544
00:29:45,533 --> 00:29:47,535
[intriguing music continues faintly]

545
00:29:54,626 --> 00:29:56,127
[distortion noise]

546
00:29:57,504 --> 00:30:00,131
[audio rumbling]

547
00:30:03,092 --> 00:30:05,220
[audio rumbling]

548
00:30:09,390 --> 00:30:11,810
No. I can't hear it.

549
00:30:11,893 --> 00:30:13,728
You can't hear anything?

550
00:30:13,812 --> 00:30:15,480
[doctor] I think it’s the device.

551
00:30:16,189 --> 00:30:18,274
The old ones were better.

552
00:30:19,901 --> 00:30:21,194
I'll get another one.

553
00:30:23,738 --> 00:30:26,074
I told you we should have come in sooner.

554
00:30:27,450 --> 00:30:29,536
[actress]
Arturo, I wanted to come sooner.

555
00:30:29,619 --> 00:30:30,912
[Arturo groans]

556
00:30:32,413 --> 00:30:34,833
Arturo. Arturo.

557
00:30:34,916 --> 00:30:36,084
[Arturo] What?

558
00:30:36,793 --> 00:30:38,670
-It’s just--
-[Arturo] It's just what?

559
00:30:38,753 --> 00:30:40,129
I just…

560
00:30:40,213 --> 00:30:41,589
[door closes]

561
00:30:44,926 --> 00:30:46,052
Let's see.

562
00:30:46,553 --> 00:30:47,720
If I may.

563
00:31:05,738 --> 00:31:06,865
There it is.

564
00:31:06,948 --> 00:31:09,951
[music becomes quiet and suspenseful]

565
00:31:10,034 --> 00:31:11,369
Good.

566
00:31:11,953 --> 00:31:13,663
-[Arturo] So, doctor…
-[exhales deeply]

567
00:31:13,746 --> 00:31:15,832
…everything's fine with my baby, right?

568
00:31:15,915 --> 00:31:18,960
Yes, yes.
I'll grant you your maternity leave.

569
00:31:22,255 --> 00:31:25,550
[Alejandra] <i>The doctor gave me</i>
<i>90 days of maternity leave,</i>

570
00:31:25,633 --> 00:31:27,886
<i>so Arturo was relieved.</i>

571
00:31:28,386 --> 00:31:31,097
<i>I was, I mean, really, at that point,</i>

572
00:31:31,180 --> 00:31:34,350
<i>-I wasn't Alejandra anymore.</i>
-[exhales deeply]

573
00:31:34,434 --> 00:31:38,605
<i>I mean, Alejandra, at that point,</i>
<i>was a mixture of everything.</i>

574
00:31:38,688 --> 00:31:41,190
<i>I was sick, I mean, I was not well.</i>

575
00:31:41,274 --> 00:31:43,902
[lively classical music playing]

576
00:31:43,985 --> 00:31:45,194
[camera shutter clicks]

577
00:31:46,863 --> 00:31:50,742
<i>In my head I was saying,</i>
<i>"What if I actually am pregnant?"</i>

578
00:31:50,825 --> 00:31:53,953
<i>"What if I didn't have a miscarriage</i>
<i>or maybe I got pregnant again?"</i>

579
00:31:54,037 --> 00:31:56,539
<i>"If I'm pregnant, how am I gonna do this?"</i>

580
00:31:56,623 --> 00:31:59,584
<i>There was a lot going on in my head</i>
<i>that wasn't right.</i>

581
00:32:00,501 --> 00:32:03,630
[woman] Well done!
Okay, now we'll do it one more time.

582
00:32:03,713 --> 00:32:05,214
[music fades]

583
00:32:08,051 --> 00:32:10,094
-Going out?
-To the hospital.

584
00:32:10,970 --> 00:32:13,890
Why are you going to work, babe?
Thought you were on leave.

585
00:32:14,557 --> 00:32:17,602
You don't have to go.
You're giving birth soon. It'll end badly.

586
00:32:17,685 --> 00:32:20,021
It's good for me to go. It's distracting.

587
00:32:20,104 --> 00:32:23,691
And besides, my quarterly report is today.
I have to help my colleagues.

588
00:32:23,775 --> 00:32:26,653
-And what am I gonna do here?
-You'll rest. You need to rest.

589
00:32:26,736 --> 00:32:28,988
I can't let them fly solo.
I have to help them.

590
00:32:29,072 --> 00:32:31,240
-They don't know how to do it.
-So what if they can't.

591
00:32:31,324 --> 00:32:33,868
-You need to be careful.
-No, I can't miss it.

592
00:32:34,369 --> 00:32:37,705
And like your mom says,
"Pregnancy is not a malady," hm?

593
00:32:38,873 --> 00:32:39,958
Fine then.

594
00:32:40,625 --> 00:32:42,669
But don't hurt my baby, okay?

595
00:32:42,752 --> 00:32:44,837
BIRTH LOG
HOSPITAL RECORDS

596
00:32:44,921 --> 00:32:46,839
PATIENT NAME - TYPE OF BIRTH

597
00:32:46,923 --> 00:32:48,967
[suspenseful music playing]

598
00:32:49,050 --> 00:32:50,259
Hi, my love.

599
00:32:51,511 --> 00:32:53,388
-Ah!
-Hi, Ale! How've you been?

600
00:32:53,471 --> 00:32:56,057
-Oh my God, great, and you?
-Good.

601
00:32:56,140 --> 00:32:59,602
Can you check on my neighbor?
She should be in now.

602
00:33:00,103 --> 00:33:02,230
Sure. Let's see, what's her name?

603
00:33:02,814 --> 00:33:05,316
[actress]
Her name is Mayra Navarro Vega.

604
00:33:05,400 --> 00:33:06,359
Mayra?

605
00:33:06,442 --> 00:33:09,946
-Mm-hm. My neighbor told me she was due.
-[nurse] Let's see.

606
00:33:10,780 --> 00:33:13,825
Mayra, Mayra…
Let’s see. Let's see. Yes, here she is.

607
00:33:13,908 --> 00:33:17,245
She came today, but they scheduled her
for a C-section tomorrow.

608
00:33:24,836 --> 00:33:27,046
[music fades]

609
00:33:27,130 --> 00:33:29,549
-[Arturo] Let's make a video for the baby.
-No.

610
00:33:29,632 --> 00:33:31,050
-Come on.
-I'm too tired.

611
00:33:31,134 --> 00:33:32,719
The baby could come tomorrow.

612
00:33:32,802 --> 00:33:35,680
No, tomorrow they’ll tell me
if they're going to induce labor.

613
00:33:35,763 --> 00:33:37,557
-Fine.
-Hey.

614
00:33:37,640 --> 00:33:40,184
-Huh?
-I'm craving chocolate. Can you get it?

615
00:33:40,268 --> 00:33:41,561
Yeah, just a minute.

616
00:33:44,772 --> 00:33:45,773
You ready?

617
00:33:46,357 --> 00:33:49,485
-Our baby's coming tomorrow.
-Mm-hm.

618
00:33:50,278 --> 00:33:51,988
[Arturo] Aren't you excited?

619
00:33:52,947 --> 00:33:55,241
So much I can't even show it.

620
00:33:55,324 --> 00:33:57,368
[Arturo] Let's see that big belly.

621
00:33:57,452 --> 00:34:00,830
When they see this video
in about ten years,

622
00:34:00,913 --> 00:34:03,207
they'll see how big your belly was.

623
00:34:03,833 --> 00:34:05,752
My baby is in there.

624
00:34:07,045 --> 00:34:08,838
My son! [chuckles]

625
00:34:09,922 --> 00:34:12,258
Everyone's gonna come see him.

626
00:34:12,759 --> 00:34:15,595
He’s gonna live here with us

627
00:34:16,095 --> 00:34:17,346
in this home.

628
00:34:18,556 --> 00:34:21,350
The one we bought, just for him.

629
00:34:23,811 --> 00:34:24,896
Right?

630
00:34:24,979 --> 00:34:27,273
[quite mystical music playing]

631
00:34:39,077 --> 00:34:41,704
PEOPLE IN RECOVERY ROOMS

632
00:34:41,788 --> 00:34:44,207
MAYRA A. NAVARRO V.
CESAREAN SECTION

633
00:34:46,334 --> 00:34:49,462
[distant babies crying]

634
00:34:51,130 --> 00:34:53,216
[music fades]

635
00:34:54,884 --> 00:34:56,511
[cell phone vibrating]

636
00:34:59,055 --> 00:35:00,765
ARTURO
CALL REJECTED

637
00:35:05,645 --> 00:35:07,105
Ale, how are you?

638
00:35:07,188 --> 00:35:08,314
Hi, sweetie.

639
00:35:08,397 --> 00:35:11,359
-What are you doing here?
-I came to see my neighbor, yeah?

640
00:35:11,442 --> 00:35:13,277
-I'll find you in a bit, okay?
-Yes!

641
00:35:16,322 --> 00:35:19,951
[Alejandra] <i>I went upstairs</i>
<i>to see Mayra around 12:30</i>

642
00:35:20,451 --> 00:35:22,286
<i>when they took her to her room.</i>

643
00:35:22,370 --> 00:35:24,372
[quiet dramatic music playing]

644
00:35:29,043 --> 00:35:30,044
Mayra.

645
00:35:30,128 --> 00:35:31,546
Where is she?

646
00:35:33,047 --> 00:35:34,215
Over there.

647
00:35:40,805 --> 00:35:43,975
[gentle heartfelt music playing]

648
00:35:44,058 --> 00:35:46,060
[actress] She's so pretty.

649
00:35:48,646 --> 00:35:50,648
She's so fair, isn't she?

650
00:35:50,731 --> 00:35:51,732
Hi.

651
00:35:55,069 --> 00:35:57,029
Hi. [chuckles]

652
00:35:58,614 --> 00:36:00,408
[Alejandra (actress) chuckles]

653
00:36:06,455 --> 00:36:08,291
[music fades]

654
00:36:08,875 --> 00:36:10,668
Our deal is still on, right?

655
00:36:11,586 --> 00:36:12,587
Yeah.

656
00:36:15,131 --> 00:36:16,924
-You okay?
-I'm cold.

657
00:36:17,675 --> 00:36:20,678
-I want to go to the bathroom.
-I'll give you my sweater.

658
00:36:21,179 --> 00:36:22,221
One second.

659
00:36:23,306 --> 00:36:24,307
There.

660
00:36:31,230 --> 00:36:33,608
[baby cooing]

661
00:36:35,943 --> 00:36:37,778
I'm going to pick her up.

662
00:36:37,862 --> 00:36:39,030
[Mayra] That's fine.

663
00:36:47,955 --> 00:36:50,249
[gentle heartfelt music resumes]

664
00:37:06,057 --> 00:37:07,308
[actress] Hello.

665
00:37:08,476 --> 00:37:10,102
[cooing]

666
00:37:11,229 --> 00:37:13,189
You sweet baby.

667
00:37:15,775 --> 00:37:17,401
Hey, baby girl.

668
00:37:18,402 --> 00:37:19,695
[door closes]

669
00:37:30,164 --> 00:37:33,042
-Shh, it's okay.
-[baby coos]

670
00:37:33,125 --> 00:37:34,752
Shh.

671
00:37:35,461 --> 00:37:36,796
How are you?

672
00:37:36,879 --> 00:37:38,172
[groans faintly]

673
00:37:38,256 --> 00:37:39,423
I'm fine.

674
00:37:41,133 --> 00:37:43,302
Did they tell you
how much the baby weighed?

675
00:37:44,053 --> 00:37:45,471
About two kilos.

676
00:37:46,973 --> 00:37:48,641
So cute.

677
00:37:48,724 --> 00:37:53,729
[Alejandra] <i>I was holding her when</i>
<i>at around two or three in the afternoon…</i>

678
00:37:53,813 --> 00:37:55,815
[man] Hi. How are you?

679
00:37:55,898 --> 00:37:57,733
[Alejandra] <i>…this man shows up.</i>

680
00:37:57,817 --> 00:37:59,151
What are you doing here?

681
00:37:59,235 --> 00:38:01,737
[tense music playing]

682
00:38:03,030 --> 00:38:04,490
There's your little girl.

683
00:38:05,366 --> 00:38:06,784
That's my daughter?

684
00:38:07,368 --> 00:38:10,079
-Why is she holding her?
-He's the baby's dad?

685
00:38:10,663 --> 00:38:12,748
-Yeah.
-[man] Let me see.

686
00:38:17,086 --> 00:38:18,504
What's going on?

687
00:38:19,714 --> 00:38:21,382
Mayra has a high fever.

688
00:38:22,591 --> 00:38:24,343
[man] Well, go tell someone.

689
00:38:25,094 --> 00:38:27,346
I'm not a doctor,
I don't know what's wrong.

690
00:38:30,474 --> 00:38:32,143
Hey there, little one.

691
00:38:32,643 --> 00:38:34,520
I'm going to get diapers for her.

692
00:38:34,603 --> 00:38:35,896
[music stops]

693
00:38:38,024 --> 00:38:41,736
[cell phone vibrates]

694
00:38:50,453 --> 00:38:52,496
-Hi, love. Sorry.
-[Arturo] <i>Why aren't you answering?</i>

695
00:38:52,580 --> 00:38:56,167
<i>I've been calling you. Where are you?</i>
<i>Are they getting you ready to give birth?</i>

696
00:38:56,250 --> 00:38:57,835
No, I'm not giving birth yet.

697
00:38:57,918 --> 00:39:00,713
<i>Tell me what the doctors are saying.</i>
<i>Tell me what's going on.</i>

698
00:39:00,796 --> 00:39:02,381
Let me speak, Arturo.

699
00:39:02,465 --> 00:39:05,926
What do you mean, what the doctors
are saying? I'm not dilated enough.

700
00:39:06,010 --> 00:39:10,306
-They're seeing if it'll be a C-section.
<i>-When are they doing the C-section?</i>

701
00:39:10,389 --> 00:39:14,185
<i>I'm still at work. My boss hasn't told me</i>
<i>if I can leave early or not.</i>

702
00:39:14,268 --> 00:39:16,520
<i>But I'll be there</i>
<i>as soon as I can. I'm coming.</i>

703
00:39:16,604 --> 00:39:19,857
No, it's not necessary
for you to come, Arturo. I'm okay.

704
00:39:19,940 --> 00:39:23,235
I'm not able to talk right now
but I’ll keep you updated.

705
00:39:31,035 --> 00:39:33,579
-Did he leave?
-[Mayra] He's gonna regret it.

706
00:39:33,662 --> 00:39:36,957
I swear, that motherfucker's gonna pay.
He's gonna pay for this.

707
00:39:37,792 --> 00:39:40,920
[fussing]

708
00:39:44,965 --> 00:39:47,968
[actress] Okay. Okay. No. No.

709
00:39:48,052 --> 00:39:50,388
Shh. Shh. Shh. Shh. Shh.

710
00:39:51,180 --> 00:39:54,934
-Okay. Time to change the baby.
-[Mayra] I have to go.

711
00:39:55,017 --> 00:39:56,727
I can't be here anymore.

712
00:39:56,811 --> 00:40:00,231
-What do you mean? Where are you going?
-[quiet tense music playing]

713
00:40:00,314 --> 00:40:01,982
Take the baby like we agreed.

714
00:40:02,066 --> 00:40:05,277
My mom won’t let me back in the house.
I have to go to Chihuahua.

715
00:40:05,361 --> 00:40:09,073
Look, Mayra, calm down.
The baby can't stay here alone.

716
00:40:09,156 --> 00:40:10,866
We have to do things properly.

717
00:40:10,950 --> 00:40:13,994
No, no, where are you going, Mayra.
Wait. No, just wait.

718
00:40:14,078 --> 00:40:15,830
I already did everything I had to.

719
00:40:16,330 --> 00:40:19,250
There’s the baby.
Isn't that’s what you wanted. Take her.

720
00:40:27,633 --> 00:40:32,096
[Alejandra] <i>I picked up the baby, went</i>
<i>into the hallway and turned around like,</i>

721
00:40:32,179 --> 00:40:33,514
<i>"No, I can't."</i>

722
00:40:33,597 --> 00:40:36,225
<i>"Even though I work</i>
<i>at the hospital and everything,</i>

723
00:40:36,308 --> 00:40:39,937
<i>there's no way I can just leave</i>
<i>with the baby like this."</i>

724
00:40:40,020 --> 00:40:42,731
[ethereal music playing]

725
00:40:44,733 --> 00:40:47,153
<i>And that's when I thought,</i>

726
00:40:47,236 --> 00:40:49,363
<i>"I better go, I'm leaving."</i>

727
00:40:50,614 --> 00:40:53,993
<i>And I swear, I said,</i>
<i>"Enough, that's enough."</i>

728
00:40:59,748 --> 00:41:01,709
<i>But I turned around and thought,</i>

729
00:41:01,792 --> 00:41:04,837
"If I leave the baby here,
what usually happens is,

730
00:41:04,920 --> 00:41:08,674
<i>because unfortunately,</i>
<i>babies are abandoned at hospitals,</i>

731
00:41:08,757 --> 00:41:11,093
<i>if I leave the baby,</i>
<i>child services takes her."</i>

732
00:41:11,177 --> 00:41:12,636
<i>"She doesn't deserve that."</i>

733
00:41:12,720 --> 00:41:16,432
<i>"Just because I messed up?</i>
<i>But how am I gonna get her out?"</i>

734
00:41:16,515 --> 00:41:19,185
[baby fussing]

735
00:41:47,296 --> 00:41:50,049
[suspenseful music playing]

736
00:41:58,807 --> 00:42:00,434
-Ale, are you leaving?
-Yeah.

737
00:42:00,518 --> 00:42:01,560
Get rest!

738
00:42:09,443 --> 00:42:11,904
[cooing]

739
00:42:25,668 --> 00:42:27,169
[man chatters]

740
00:42:30,548 --> 00:42:31,799
[Alejandra] <i>I left the hospital,</i>

741
00:42:32,758 --> 00:42:34,510
<i>and that’s when… I don't know.</i>

742
00:42:35,636 --> 00:42:38,681
<i>Maybe it was fate</i>
<i>or maybe it was just luck.</i>

743
00:42:38,764 --> 00:42:40,015
<i>I don't know.</i>

744
00:42:41,350 --> 00:42:44,395
<i>I was walking out and I heard someone say,</i>

745
00:42:44,895 --> 00:42:46,772
<i>"What are you doing? Alejandra."</i>

746
00:42:46,855 --> 00:42:48,732
Alejandra! What happened?

747
00:42:48,816 --> 00:42:49,900
[music stops]

748
00:42:49,984 --> 00:42:51,318
What happened?

749
00:42:51,402 --> 00:42:53,028
I already gave birth.

750
00:42:53,112 --> 00:42:55,990
What are you thinking?
What happened? Why'd you leave?

751
00:42:56,073 --> 00:42:59,577
Arturo, calm down, seriously.
Everything went well. The birth was fine.

752
00:42:59,660 --> 00:43:02,621
What happened, Alejandra?
Tell me what happened.

753
00:43:14,174 --> 00:43:15,759
I lost our child, okay?

754
00:43:16,343 --> 00:43:18,178
-What?
-I lost our baby months ago.

755
00:43:18,262 --> 00:43:20,306
What do you mean, you lost the baby?

756
00:43:21,390 --> 00:43:22,516
How could…?

757
00:43:27,021 --> 00:43:28,147
Look.

758
00:43:29,106 --> 00:43:32,026
-They gave me this baby.
-[gasps] What? Are you serious?

759
00:43:32,109 --> 00:43:34,194
-[gasping]
-Arturo! Arturo!

760
00:43:34,278 --> 00:43:37,740
Listen to me. They gave her to me!
Arturo, they gave her to me.

761
00:43:37,823 --> 00:43:40,409
-What'll I do with you? You're crazy.
-What do you mean?

762
00:43:40,492 --> 00:43:42,995
-Get out and give them that baby.
-I'm not going!

763
00:43:43,078 --> 00:43:44,955
-Take her back!
-I'm not taking her back!

764
00:43:45,039 --> 00:43:48,042
-Take that baby back. Get out of the car!
-I'm not taking her back!

765
00:43:48,125 --> 00:43:51,253
-I'm not taking her back!
-People don't give babies away! Get out.

766
00:43:51,337 --> 00:43:52,921
Get the fuck out of here!

767
00:43:58,093 --> 00:44:00,929
Arturo, please, listen to me. Arturo.

768
00:44:01,013 --> 00:44:03,766
Arturo, just…
I am telling you, I am begging you.

769
00:44:04,391 --> 00:44:07,353
The baby didn't do anything.
What will happen to her?

770
00:44:08,103 --> 00:44:11,607
-Arturo, I’m talking to you! Listen to me!
-[anguished groaning]

771
00:44:11,690 --> 00:44:13,984
Ah! Fine, get in!

772
00:44:14,068 --> 00:44:18,489
EXIT

773
00:44:28,916 --> 00:44:30,334
What are you gonna do?

774
00:44:31,377 --> 00:44:32,419
Well…

775
00:44:32,961 --> 00:44:36,006
It's just that Mayra,
the baby's mom, leaves early tomorrow.

776
00:44:36,924 --> 00:44:40,636
I was going to pretend to be a family
member so they would let her go home.

777
00:44:41,136 --> 00:44:45,265
And then, when you guys got there, I would
already have the baby and paperwork.

778
00:44:45,349 --> 00:44:48,018
That's it, Arturo.
I didn't think this would happen.

779
00:44:48,519 --> 00:44:50,688
-This just isn't right.
-Forgive me.

780
00:44:51,522 --> 00:44:54,191
I love you, Arturo.
Please, please forgive me.

781
00:44:54,692 --> 00:44:57,236
-Don't leave, my love.
-So that's why you lied then?

782
00:44:58,946 --> 00:45:00,489
They couldn't find me out.

783
00:45:01,532 --> 00:45:02,991
What would they say?

784
00:45:03,075 --> 00:45:06,578
-Someone just gave her away.
-Why'd you keep me in the dark, Alejandra?

785
00:45:07,663 --> 00:45:11,250
What are you getting me into, dammit?
I don't know. I don't know.

786
00:45:11,333 --> 00:45:12,793
[baby fussing]

787
00:45:12,876 --> 00:45:14,670
Shh. Shh.

788
00:45:14,753 --> 00:45:16,672
-It's okay, it's okay.
-[gasps]

789
00:45:29,351 --> 00:45:32,229
I don't care how you do it,
but I want my child, okay?

790
00:45:34,356 --> 00:45:37,067
[baby coos]

791
00:45:46,201 --> 00:45:48,495
-You're okay.
-[baby fusses]

792
00:45:50,998 --> 00:45:52,374
Give her to me.

793
00:45:55,419 --> 00:45:56,920
-[baby fusses]
-It's okay.

794
00:45:59,339 --> 00:46:01,759
-It's okay.
-[fussing]

795
00:46:02,634 --> 00:46:03,886
It's okay.

796
00:46:05,387 --> 00:46:08,432
-[crying]
-No, no, don't be scared.

797
00:46:08,515 --> 00:46:11,351
[quiet ethereal music playing]

798
00:46:13,187 --> 00:46:15,355
[cooing]

799
00:46:18,567 --> 00:46:20,110
It's okay, baby.

800
00:47:12,746 --> 00:47:13,747
[kiss]

801
00:47:19,378 --> 00:47:21,380
[music fades]

802
00:47:23,090 --> 00:47:25,384
-[officer 1] Police!
-[officer 2] Police! Hands up!

803
00:47:25,467 --> 00:47:27,970
-What happened?!
-[officer 1] Hands where I can see them!

804
00:47:28,053 --> 00:47:31,265
-We didn't do anything!
-[officer shouting indistinctly]

805
00:47:31,348 --> 00:47:32,266
[officer] Move it!

806
00:47:32,349 --> 00:47:35,727
-No, no, no! Let go of me!
-Hey, calm down. Okay?

807
00:47:35,811 --> 00:47:38,730
-We're going to get her checked out.
-I'm her mama!

808
00:47:38,814 --> 00:47:41,984
-Arturo, my daughter! I'm her mama!
-Nothing's going to happen.

809
00:47:42,067 --> 00:47:45,487
-[officer] Going to see if she's okay.
-[baby cries]

810
00:47:45,571 --> 00:47:47,823
Ale, just do it! Just give her to 'em!

811
00:47:47,906 --> 00:47:50,701
That's it, hand her over, slowly.

812
00:47:50,784 --> 00:47:53,161
-[officer 2] We've got the girl back.
-Let her go!

813
00:47:53,245 --> 00:47:56,707
-Let her go, you bastard! Let her go!
-[baby continues crying]

814
00:47:56,790 --> 00:47:58,375
Stop hurting her, asshole!

815
00:47:58,458 --> 00:48:00,752
[officer 2] Shut your mouth! You hear me?

816
00:48:00,836 --> 00:48:03,005
-Identify yourself!
-Arturo Calderón Gamino!

817
00:48:03,088 --> 00:48:04,506
And you? And you?!

818
00:48:04,590 --> 00:48:06,967
[Arturo] She's Eleonor
Alejandra Marín Mendoza!

819
00:48:07,050 --> 00:48:09,511
[officer 1] Eleonor
Alejandra Marín Mendoza!

820
00:48:09,595 --> 00:48:12,347
[moody music playing]

821
00:48:12,431 --> 00:48:14,892
[chatter over police radio]

822
00:48:37,873 --> 00:48:40,459
[radio host] <i>We're playing songs</i>
<i>from the past.</i>

823
00:48:40,542 --> 00:48:43,587
<i>For the romantics, we have this classic.</i>

824
00:48:43,670 --> 00:48:46,673
["Unchained Melody"
by The Righteous Brothers playing]

825
00:48:50,969 --> 00:48:54,097
[Alejandra] <i>We were in the squad car,</i>
<i>and that song started playing.</i>

826
00:48:54,181 --> 00:48:56,642
<i>And the fact that we danced to it</i>
<i>on our wedding day,</i>

827
00:48:56,725 --> 00:48:59,102
<i>that it was our special dance,</i>

828
00:48:59,186 --> 00:49:02,522
<i>and to be hearing it then was like…</i>

829
00:49:04,191 --> 00:49:07,778
<i>I don't know, like for me, I felt like</i>

830
00:49:09,029 --> 00:49:11,531
<i>love is real and we were gonna be okay.</i>

831
00:49:11,615 --> 00:49:12,950
<i>That's how I felt.</i>

832
00:49:13,033 --> 00:49:15,786
<i>♪ And time ♪</i>

833
00:49:15,869 --> 00:49:18,455
<i>♪ Goes by ♪</i>

834
00:49:18,538 --> 00:49:20,832
Sir, please, would you turn off that song?

835
00:49:20,916 --> 00:49:22,876
Sir, please turn off that song!

836
00:49:23,877 --> 00:49:27,214
Please, for the love of God, turn it off.
Please, just turn it off.

837
00:49:27,923 --> 00:49:29,257
[gasps]

838
00:49:30,092 --> 00:49:32,094
[moody whimsical music playing]

839
00:49:46,274 --> 00:49:48,777
-[reporters] Ale!
-[overlapping shouting]

840
00:49:48,860 --> 00:49:50,612
[reporter 1] Can we get a picture?

841
00:49:50,696 --> 00:49:52,572
[overlapping chatter continues]

842
00:49:55,784 --> 00:49:58,704
-[reporter 2] Did your husband help?
-[reporter 3] Plan everything together?

843
00:49:58,787 --> 00:50:02,207
No, my husband had nothing
to do with this. And I'm not a thief.

844
00:50:04,376 --> 00:50:06,628
I made arrangements
with the girl's mother.

845
00:50:07,504 --> 00:50:10,007
Five months ago I saw her at the hospital.

846
00:50:10,090 --> 00:50:12,467
We both talked at the clinic,

847
00:50:12,551 --> 00:50:14,386
her and I, so…

848
00:50:14,469 --> 00:50:17,764
She said she was a mother and single,
that it was her second child,

849
00:50:17,848 --> 00:50:20,934
with a different father,
and that she wanted to abort it.

850
00:50:21,018 --> 00:50:24,021
She told me she wanted
to get rid of it or give it away.

851
00:50:24,104 --> 00:50:26,606
She assured me
she knew what she wanted to do with it,

852
00:50:26,690 --> 00:50:28,108
so I asked to be considered.

853
00:50:28,191 --> 00:50:30,861
[reporter 2] If you two had
an arrangement, why did you take the baby?

854
00:50:30,944 --> 00:50:33,405
[reporter 4]
Arturo, were you part of the plan?

855
00:50:33,488 --> 00:50:36,116
{\an8}FEDERAL DISTRICT'S DEPARTMENT OF JUSTICE

856
00:50:36,199 --> 00:50:38,410
{\an8}[news anchor 1]
<i>They call her the baby snatcher.</i>

857
00:50:38,493 --> 00:50:41,705
{\an8}<i>Authorities believe she had help</i>
<i>from her husband, Arturo Calderón.</i>

858
00:50:41,788 --> 00:50:44,666
[news anchor 2]
<i>…Mendoza and Arturo Calderón Gamino</i>

859
00:50:44,750 --> 00:50:47,586
<i>the two suspects accused</i>
<i>of abducting a baby.</i>

860
00:50:47,669 --> 00:50:50,672
[news anchor 3] <i>They stole the newborn</i>
<i>from Mexico General Hospital</i>

861
00:50:50,756 --> 00:50:53,884
<i>while the parents were left</i>
<i>with overwhelming despair.</i>

862
00:51:01,892 --> 00:51:05,228
["En Otra Vida"
by Yami Safdie & Lasso playing]

863
00:51:15,530 --> 00:51:19,534
[n Spanish] ♪ <i>In another life </i>♪

864
00:51:19,618 --> 00:51:23,413
<i>♪ We got married</i>
<i>And traveled all over the world ♪</i>

865
00:51:23,497 --> 00:51:27,167
<i>♪ We moved to a flat on the second floor ♪</i>

866
00:51:27,250 --> 00:51:31,546
♪ <i>My parents</i>
<i>And your parents are friends </i>♪

867
00:51:32,798 --> 00:51:34,966
♪ <i>Our children </i>♪

868
00:51:35,050 --> 00:51:38,929
♪ <i>Have my patience and your smile </i>♪

869
00:51:39,012 --> 00:51:42,724
<i>♪ We go for strolls</i>
<i>And we read poetry ♪</i>

870
00:51:42,808 --> 00:51:47,104
♪ <i>Shit, we had a great other life </i>♪

871
00:51:48,313 --> 00:51:50,398
♪ <i>Not this one </i>♪

872
00:51:50,482 --> 00:51:54,361
♪ <i>I don’t know why it didn’t work out </i>♪

873
00:51:54,444 --> 00:51:58,156
♪ <i>Maybe it was a whim of God </i>♪

874
00:51:58,240 --> 00:52:04,037
♪ <i>The courage</i>
<i>That they both always lacked </i>♪

875
00:52:04,121 --> 00:52:10,085
♪ <i>But I'll wait for you here </i>♪

876
00:52:10,168 --> 00:52:13,964
♪ <i>If you change your mind </i>♪

877
00:52:14,047 --> 00:52:17,592
♪ <i>It's not too late to return… </i>♪

878
00:52:20,220 --> 00:52:25,809
I’ve served 13 years,
3 months and 25 days in prison.

879
00:52:35,986 --> 00:52:39,739
When I first got here,
I was very hard for me.

880
00:52:40,949 --> 00:52:44,369
Because not only was Alejandra
going to jail,

881
00:52:44,452 --> 00:52:47,247
Alejandra was also being called a liar.

882
00:52:48,415 --> 00:52:50,667
Alejandra had hurt her parents.

883
00:52:51,877 --> 00:52:55,213
Alejandra had hurt her husband.

884
00:52:56,298 --> 00:52:57,924
[distant shouting]

885
00:52:58,008 --> 00:53:02,179
Alejandra had done the worst things
without meaning to.

886
00:53:14,524 --> 00:53:17,319
The first few years were hard
because Arturo, my husband,

887
00:53:17,402 --> 00:53:19,154
was considered my accomplice.

888
00:53:19,237 --> 00:53:22,949
so I felt guilty about everything
that was happening to him.

889
00:53:23,033 --> 00:53:25,911
I mean, I wanted to go through
what he was going through.

890
00:53:25,994 --> 00:53:27,746
I wanted to…

891
00:53:27,829 --> 00:53:31,082
If it was Arturo's turn
to use the bathroom at the men's prison,

892
00:53:31,166 --> 00:53:33,919
I wanted to be in the bathroom with him.

893
00:53:34,002 --> 00:53:37,756
And if he didn’t eat,
I didn't want to, stuff like that.

894
00:53:37,839 --> 00:53:44,679
{\an8}FEDERAL DISTRICT'S DEPARTMENT OF JUSTICE

895
00:53:44,763 --> 00:53:47,849
She did something unforgivable
in that moment.

896
00:53:49,809 --> 00:53:54,314
And yeah, the feeling
is rage, pretty much.

897
00:53:55,899 --> 00:53:59,736
That's the only thing that…
that I could feel toward her at the time.

898
00:54:00,570 --> 00:54:04,449
I kept thinking, "Will this have
consequences, legally speaking,

899
00:54:04,532 --> 00:54:07,494
or, like, kill my love for her?"

900
00:54:07,577 --> 00:54:10,413
"Or should I just divorce Alejandra
because of this lie?"

901
00:54:10,497 --> 00:54:12,207
[heartfelt music playing]

902
00:54:12,290 --> 00:54:14,793
"Because she deceived me
because this is not my baby,

903
00:54:14,876 --> 00:54:17,462
because she did things
she shouldn't have?"

904
00:54:17,545 --> 00:54:21,216
"Or because she's not a good wife,"
and stuff like that.

905
00:54:21,299 --> 00:54:23,009
"I'll never see her again."

906
00:54:23,093 --> 00:54:25,762
That’s the only thing
I thought about while I was in jail.

907
00:54:25,845 --> 00:54:27,931
Your head is about to explode.

908
00:54:28,014 --> 00:54:29,599
I mean, the fear.

909
00:54:30,100 --> 00:54:33,687
The terror,
it later becomes terror. It's just…

910
00:54:34,229 --> 00:54:36,856
You want to cry and can't
because they will beat you up.

911
00:54:36,940 --> 00:54:39,901
Or they'll beat you up even worse
because you're crying.

912
00:54:40,735 --> 00:54:42,320
No, I mean, you're broken.

913
00:54:42,404 --> 00:54:45,448
Emotionally, physically and in every way.

914
00:54:45,949 --> 00:54:48,451
That's just part of the deal
when you go to jail.

915
00:54:48,535 --> 00:54:50,870
-[contemplative music playing]
-[woman shouting]

916
00:54:50,954 --> 00:54:52,872
[woman 1] Like that other shade.

917
00:54:52,956 --> 00:54:54,708
I like this shade.

918
00:54:54,791 --> 00:54:57,585
Here are the others.
I'll give you the other one later.

919
00:54:59,587 --> 00:55:02,340
[woman 1] Go for a 4.1 or a 5.1

920
00:55:02,882 --> 00:55:05,176
Oh, don't talk to Arturo,
baby, because you won't.

921
00:55:05,760 --> 00:55:09,514
[Alejandra] Yesterday, when I called
Arturo, he was really intense.

922
00:55:09,597 --> 00:55:10,557
[woman 2] I heard.

923
00:55:10,640 --> 00:55:12,726
Oh, you were inside already?

924
00:55:12,809 --> 00:55:14,269
-So you heard.
-[woman 2] What?

925
00:55:14,352 --> 00:55:17,605
He got intense last night.
I called him and I'm like, "Hi, honey--"

926
00:55:17,689 --> 00:55:19,691
[woman 2] He's going through andropause.

927
00:55:19,774 --> 00:55:21,693
I said, "Hi, honey. How are you?"

928
00:55:21,776 --> 00:55:24,654
And he says, "Hi. Fine, and you?"

929
00:55:25,196 --> 00:55:28,116
And I say, "Fine, hon. What's up?"

930
00:55:28,199 --> 00:55:29,326
"I'm mad."

931
00:55:29,826 --> 00:55:31,202
[woman 2] Poor sweet thing.

932
00:55:31,286 --> 00:55:34,331
[woman 1] His heart is aching.
You have to give in a little too.

933
00:55:34,414 --> 00:55:36,082
You just want him to give in?

934
00:55:36,166 --> 00:55:39,419
So what am I gonna do? Whatever he wants?

935
00:55:40,545 --> 00:55:41,796
[woman 2] Beats me, girl.

936
00:55:41,880 --> 00:55:43,840
{\an8}Hurray for women's liberation.

937
00:55:43,923 --> 00:55:46,468
-[all laugh]
-[Alejandra] Just that he always wins.

938
00:55:46,551 --> 00:55:49,679
[woman 2] You won't…
You won't be able to control him anymore.

939
00:55:50,221 --> 00:55:52,515
-No one values how hard he tries.
-Oh, no.

940
00:55:52,599 --> 00:55:55,685
[news program music playing]

941
00:55:57,687 --> 00:56:01,733
Pay attention, because this investigation
has two possible theories.

942
00:56:01,816 --> 00:56:03,943
First, is that the girl was stolen.

943
00:56:04,027 --> 00:56:07,113
Second hypothesis
is that she was given away.

944
00:56:07,197 --> 00:56:08,281
But why?

945
00:56:08,365 --> 00:56:10,784
At the time of her arrest,
this woman testified

946
00:56:10,867 --> 00:56:14,412
that the baby was given away
by her birth mother.

947
00:56:14,954 --> 00:56:17,665
Five months ago,
I met her at the hospital.

948
00:56:18,166 --> 00:56:22,796
We were at the clinic when we had
our first conversation, her and I.

949
00:56:23,713 --> 00:56:26,049
She tells me she was a single mother,

950
00:56:26,132 --> 00:56:28,760
her second child with a different father,

951
00:56:29,427 --> 00:56:31,304
and that she wanted an abortion.

952
00:56:31,888 --> 00:56:36,810
She told me that she either wanted
to get rid of it or give away the baby.

953
00:56:36,893 --> 00:56:38,436
{\an8}REPORT OF SUSPICIOUS COUPLE
WITH A BABY

954
00:56:38,520 --> 00:56:41,981
{\an8}[news anchor] <i>Eleonor is blaming</i>
<i>the newborn’s mother.</i>

955
00:56:42,482 --> 00:56:44,859
<i>She said that they had made a deal</i>

956
00:56:44,943 --> 00:56:47,654
<i>that she would give her the baby.</i>

957
00:56:48,279 --> 00:56:51,282
[Mayra] I felt guilty
for leaving her alone.

958
00:56:51,783 --> 00:56:53,368
It was awful.

959
00:56:53,451 --> 00:56:55,578
Desperation, anguish…

960
00:56:55,662 --> 00:56:57,539
I wanted to hug her.

961
00:56:58,623 --> 00:57:01,543
I hope she forgives me
for leaving her alone.

962
00:57:01,626 --> 00:57:05,797
The justice system will be responsible
for shedding light on what happened

963
00:57:05,880 --> 00:57:09,134
and, of course,
for punishing those responsible.

964
00:57:10,093 --> 00:57:13,096
As a judge, you can’t, um…

965
00:57:14,431 --> 00:57:17,642
dismiss a version of the facts

966
00:57:18,601 --> 00:57:21,271
under the premise that,
"Oh, this is incredible,"

967
00:57:21,354 --> 00:57:24,691
or "No, it’s impossible
that this happened."

968
00:57:24,774 --> 00:57:27,193
"No, this doesn’t happen in real life."

969
00:57:27,277 --> 00:57:31,281
Let's just say
that more things happen in real life

970
00:57:31,364 --> 00:57:34,075
than fiction could ever envision.

971
00:57:34,617 --> 00:57:36,578
So, it was possible.

972
00:57:36,661 --> 00:57:40,874
It was possible that she had an agreement
with the girl's mother.

973
00:57:40,957 --> 00:57:42,000
{\an8}EVIDENCE

974
00:57:42,083 --> 00:57:46,963
{\an8}And we, the judges,
beyond the positions that people may have,

975
00:57:47,046 --> 00:57:50,675
{\an8}the truth is that everything is subject
to how it is proven,

976
00:57:50,758 --> 00:57:54,846
{\an8}or rather, whether it is proven
during the trial itself.

977
00:57:55,930 --> 00:57:58,558
EVIDENCE

978
00:57:59,726 --> 00:58:02,145
{\an8}[Alejandra] The wedding veil,
what do you think?

979
00:58:04,022 --> 00:58:05,857
{\an8}[Arturo] The other thing
I want you to wear--

980
00:58:05,940 --> 00:58:09,444
{\an8}[judge] At the trial,
Alejandra told her story,

981
00:58:09,527 --> 00:58:12,572
{\an8}and she told it in a very consistent way.

982
00:58:13,072 --> 00:58:16,075
{\an8}regarding the suffering
that she had experienced.

983
00:58:17,410 --> 00:58:19,871
{\an8}A woman with a functional marriage,

984
00:58:19,954 --> 00:58:22,165
{\an8}but who does not feel satisfied

985
00:58:22,248 --> 00:58:26,002
{\an8}because she cannot fulfill the societal
expectation of being a mother.

986
00:58:26,085 --> 00:58:27,921
{\an8}["Unchained Melody" playing]

987
00:58:28,004 --> 00:58:30,882
{\an8}She is criticized by her husband's family,

988
00:58:30,965 --> 00:58:32,425
in the sense that…

989
00:58:33,218 --> 00:58:37,555
"Well, you are probably no good
as a woman if you aren't a mother."

990
00:58:38,598 --> 00:58:43,186
The most a woman who cannot be a mother
can evoke in us is compassion.

991
00:58:43,269 --> 00:58:46,105
In this story, as in many others,

992
00:58:46,189 --> 00:58:48,066
we see how these gender roles

993
00:58:48,149 --> 00:58:52,237
disproportionately affect women,

994
00:58:52,320 --> 00:58:56,783
leading to tragic outcomes,
as happened in this case.

995
00:58:58,660 --> 00:59:02,455
A family is the husband,

996
00:59:02,539 --> 00:59:04,749
the mother, the house,

997
00:59:05,458 --> 00:59:06,626
the car,

998
00:59:07,293 --> 00:59:08,378
and the children.

999
00:59:09,587 --> 00:59:13,967
And I think all of that began to cause
psychological damage to my daughter.

1000
00:59:14,050 --> 00:59:16,010
[gentle contemplative music playing]

1001
00:59:16,094 --> 00:59:18,596
When I said,
"I don't want to consider adopting,"

1002
00:59:18,680 --> 00:59:21,182
I want a child with my DNA,"

1003
00:59:21,266 --> 00:59:25,603
I maybe contributed
to closing myself off in that sense."

1004
00:59:25,687 --> 00:59:28,523
At some point, I did put pressure on her

1005
00:59:29,232 --> 00:59:31,484
because I said, "I wanna be a dad."

1006
00:59:31,568 --> 00:59:34,612
"I want to be a dad,
and I want to have a kid."

1007
00:59:36,698 --> 00:59:40,285
Obviously, being in jail, you have
a lot of time to think about things,

1008
00:59:40,368 --> 00:59:44,581
to see what
or where you failed as a partner.

1009
00:59:44,664 --> 00:59:46,958
At that time, I didn't understand it,

1010
00:59:47,041 --> 00:59:49,586
I didn't justify it, I didn't get it.

1011
00:59:49,669 --> 00:59:52,630
But I was starting to soften.

1012
00:59:52,714 --> 00:59:56,843
And with the problems I've told you about,
the ones I had in jail,

1013
00:59:56,926 --> 00:59:58,720
I started to talk more with Ale.

1014
01:00:00,305 --> 01:00:03,308
"Ale, I'm sorry
I didn't write to you before."

1015
01:00:03,391 --> 01:00:06,811
"I was confused and overwhelmed,
scared and depressed."

1016
01:00:06,894 --> 01:00:10,356
"For me, it's very difficult
to justify your lie."

1017
01:00:10,440 --> 01:00:12,609
"It causes me a lot of hurt and pain."

1018
01:00:12,692 --> 01:00:14,861
"Of course, what happened
was no small thing."

1019
01:00:14,944 --> 01:00:18,197
"But even so,
I forgive you with all my heart."

1020
01:00:18,281 --> 01:00:22,118
"Hello, my love, my beauty,
my light and my everything."

1021
01:00:22,619 --> 01:00:25,872
"I hope the bedbugs let you sleep,
you sleepyhead."

1022
01:00:26,372 --> 01:00:30,335
"Hey, my love, I wanted to tell you
something, I hope you don't mind."

1023
01:00:30,418 --> 01:00:35,048
"I’m going to work really hard
to save money and be able to do IVF."

1024
01:00:35,131 --> 01:00:38,760
"I read in the newspaper that we can
probably get a surrogate, my love,

1025
01:00:38,843 --> 01:00:41,220
and that we have
to get through this nightmare."

1026
01:00:41,304 --> 01:00:43,139
"You have to be strong."

1027
01:00:43,222 --> 01:00:45,099
"I love you with all my heart."

1028
01:00:46,142 --> 01:00:48,394
I spent two years in jail.

1029
01:00:48,478 --> 01:00:50,563
Two years and six months.

1030
01:00:50,647 --> 01:00:52,690
Until the trial was over.

1031
01:00:53,399 --> 01:00:55,443
And I was acquitted.

1032
01:00:56,152 --> 01:00:59,364
All the psychological damage
you get from being in jail,

1033
01:00:59,447 --> 01:01:02,617
they just tell you,
"Your sentence is acquitted."

1034
01:01:02,700 --> 01:01:05,828
"We'll destroy your record
right here in front of you."

1035
01:01:05,912 --> 01:01:08,414
"Look, you don't have a criminal record."

1036
01:01:08,498 --> 01:01:10,291
But the scar remains.

1037
01:01:11,959 --> 01:01:15,254
What we concluded in terms
of the theory of the crime,

1038
01:01:15,338 --> 01:01:18,049
is that there was no malicious intent
on his part.

1039
01:01:18,132 --> 01:01:19,342
He wasn’t an accomplice,

1040
01:01:19,425 --> 01:01:22,929
because he was only aware of Alejandra's
version of the encounter with Mayra.

1041
01:01:24,847 --> 01:01:27,225
And that alleged agreement with Mayra

1042
01:01:27,308 --> 01:01:30,103
was the weakest part
of Alejandra's defense.

1043
01:01:31,396 --> 01:01:34,899
The General Hospital
reported the disappearance,

1044
01:01:34,982 --> 01:01:38,361
and they made the request
to call the police.

1045
01:01:38,444 --> 01:01:40,655
When the police arrived,
they talked to her,

1046
01:01:40,738 --> 01:01:43,491
and that's when she said,
"Yes, she was stolen from me."

1047
01:01:43,574 --> 01:01:46,369
I'm guessing. As I said, I don't know.

1048
01:01:46,452 --> 01:01:49,247
But it wasn't until
the hospital reported it.

1049
01:01:49,330 --> 01:01:52,417
Obviously, I know that you can't do that,

1050
01:01:52,500 --> 01:01:55,420
so it had to be her or me in prison.

1051
01:01:55,920 --> 01:01:58,423
She couldn't have said,
"I gave away the baby,"

1052
01:01:58,506 --> 01:02:00,633
because that's illegal too, right?

1053
01:02:02,218 --> 01:02:05,012
[director] Mayra, it was hard
to get your version of the story.

1054
01:02:05,096 --> 01:02:07,974
For a long time,
I had only ever heard Ale’s version,

1055
01:02:08,641 --> 01:02:12,395
who told me that you met at the General
Hospital when you were pregnant,

1056
01:02:12,478 --> 01:02:15,022
and that on the day of the birth
you left the baby

1057
01:02:15,106 --> 01:02:17,191
and told her you were going to Chihuahua.

1058
01:02:17,692 --> 01:02:19,527
What do you think of this version?

1059
01:02:20,862 --> 01:02:22,989
Well, it's very illogical.

1060
01:02:24,407 --> 01:02:26,576
Super illogical, it's very…

1061
01:02:28,411 --> 01:02:29,704
I mean,

1062
01:02:29,787 --> 01:02:31,664
If you’re going to give away a baby,

1063
01:02:31,748 --> 01:02:34,292
you wouldn't do it
inside the hospital, right?

1064
01:02:34,375 --> 01:02:36,627
You wouldn't take her the way she did.

1065
01:02:36,711 --> 01:02:39,172
[moody dramatic music playing]

1066
01:02:40,173 --> 01:02:42,258
There was never a deal, never.

1067
01:02:42,341 --> 01:02:45,595
{\an8}I'm telling you, I didn't see her
until the day Katya was born,

1068
01:02:45,678 --> 01:02:47,472
{\an8}and the evidence shows that.

1069
01:02:47,555 --> 01:02:50,933
{\an8}My pregnancy checkup records
are at the health center.

1070
01:02:51,434 --> 01:02:54,520
I only went to the hospital
to give birth, nothing else.

1071
01:02:55,563 --> 01:02:57,899
I had my pregnancy check-ups
at a health center.

1072
01:02:57,982 --> 01:03:00,568
I never set foot
in the hospital before that.

1073
01:03:01,694 --> 01:03:04,030
There is no way I could have met her.

1074
01:03:04,113 --> 01:03:06,699
PRENATAL CHECKUP

1075
01:03:06,783 --> 01:03:10,787
[judge] There were documents,
like Mayra's appointment card

1076
01:03:10,870 --> 01:03:13,956
where you could see
that her pregnancy checkups

1077
01:03:14,040 --> 01:03:15,917
were at a different clinic.

1078
01:03:16,000 --> 01:03:20,671
It wasn't until very late,
almost at the end of her pregnancy,

1079
01:03:20,755 --> 01:03:22,965
when she went to the General Hospital.

1080
01:03:23,466 --> 01:03:25,343
So, there was no correlation

1081
01:03:25,426 --> 01:03:28,888
between the circumstances
described by Alejandra

1082
01:03:29,472 --> 01:03:34,268
and the fact that, actually, Mayra had not
been physically at the hospital

1083
01:03:34,352 --> 01:03:38,147
until just a few weeks
before giving birth.

1084
01:03:38,231 --> 01:03:40,441
[intriguing music playing]

1085
01:03:41,567 --> 01:03:46,572
[Mayra] She was wandering around
the labor and delivery unit

1086
01:03:47,907 --> 01:03:51,244
and came to tell me
that she was doing a survey.

1087
01:03:51,327 --> 01:03:54,372
He showed me her ID,
her badge, and I trusted her.

1088
01:03:54,455 --> 01:03:56,707
She started asking a lot of questions.

1089
01:03:56,791 --> 01:03:58,835
She asked if it was my first daughter,

1090
01:03:58,918 --> 01:04:00,753
if this was from the same marriage,

1091
01:04:00,837 --> 01:04:05,091
and, well,
how was my relationship with the father.

1092
01:04:05,174 --> 01:04:07,426
I mean, she got everything from there.

1093
01:04:08,135 --> 01:04:11,722
Everything she told the police
was practically everything she asked me.

1094
01:04:12,765 --> 01:04:15,893
[director] Ale, what doesn’t fit
in your story is that the file says

1095
01:04:15,977 --> 01:04:19,355
you arrived at the hospital
posing as a social worker.

1096
01:04:19,438 --> 01:04:21,774
Were you conducting surveys?

1097
01:04:21,858 --> 01:04:25,319
[Alejandra] A lot of people
might say that, you know,

1098
01:04:25,403 --> 01:04:27,154
that I was doing surveys.

1099
01:04:27,238 --> 01:04:29,615
The truth is, it wasn't like that.

1100
01:04:29,699 --> 01:04:32,743
[director] You went to the maternity
ward saying you were a relative?

1101
01:04:32,827 --> 01:04:35,955
-[Alejandra] That she was my neighbor.
-I came to see a neighbor.

1102
01:04:36,038 --> 01:04:37,498
[Alejandra] Things like that.

1103
01:04:37,582 --> 01:04:41,711
That she was my neighbor,
and I had to go in to see her, and so on.

1104
01:04:43,087 --> 01:04:46,257
{\an8}ELEONOR ALEJANDRA MARÍN MENDOZA
AREA 3 - UROLOGY

1105
01:04:46,340 --> 01:04:49,802
They found the sweater
Alejandra was wearing,

1106
01:04:50,303 --> 01:04:55,099
which had the badge
with her ID as hospital worker.

1107
01:04:55,892 --> 01:04:59,645
And they also found this folder
with the surveys,

1108
01:04:59,729 --> 01:05:02,899
which were the documents
Alejandra took with her

1109
01:05:02,982 --> 01:05:05,026
to start up a conversation.

1110
01:05:06,110 --> 01:05:08,279
I went into the hospital,

1111
01:05:08,779 --> 01:05:11,073
and Mayra was in bed.

1112
01:05:11,157 --> 01:05:13,200
I asked her, "How are you feeling?"

1113
01:05:13,284 --> 01:05:16,287
She said, "Really bad.
I have a high fever."

1114
01:05:17,246 --> 01:05:19,373
And then she said, "There's the baby."

1115
01:05:19,957 --> 01:05:24,295
And, well, I saw my daughter
for the first time, and

1116
01:05:24,378 --> 01:05:25,630
I fell in love with her.

1117
01:05:25,713 --> 01:05:28,507
-[Mayra] Vale.
-[father] Okay. My girl.

1118
01:05:29,967 --> 01:05:31,427
We're asleep.

1119
01:05:33,304 --> 01:05:34,889
For when she's older.

1120
01:05:34,972 --> 01:05:39,060
I'll have the video edited so she can see
where she was when she was born.

1121
01:05:40,561 --> 01:05:44,023
[in voiceover] At that point,
when I got there to meet my daughter,

1122
01:05:44,106 --> 01:05:45,858
Mayra was with someone.

1123
01:05:45,942 --> 01:05:48,194
I said, "Mayra, who is this?"

1124
01:05:48,778 --> 01:05:53,574
And Mayra said to me, "She’s a social
worker who's doing some surveys."

1125
01:05:54,367 --> 01:05:56,744
That's when she got up and left.

1126
01:05:56,827 --> 01:05:59,830
She got up,
left the papers and walked out.

1127
01:06:00,873 --> 01:06:04,794
Around 6:00 p.m. when visiting hours
were over, I went back to the room.

1128
01:06:04,877 --> 01:06:07,296
And she had already taken a shower.

1129
01:06:07,380 --> 01:06:09,507
And I said, "Is everything okay?"

1130
01:06:10,383 --> 01:06:14,971
And she said, "Yes, but he's gonna pay
for it, that motherfucker."

1131
01:06:15,054 --> 01:06:17,556
You know what?
Keep her, just like we agreed.

1132
01:06:18,057 --> 01:06:19,433
[actress] What do you mean?

1133
01:06:19,517 --> 01:06:21,978
[Alejandra] She said to me,
"I’m going to Chihuahua."

1134
01:06:22,061 --> 01:06:24,146
-I'm going to Chihuahua.
-[actress] You can't leave.

1135
01:06:24,230 --> 01:06:27,525
And I was like, "What?
What do you mean, you're leaving?"

1136
01:06:27,608 --> 01:06:30,403
I had a fever of almost 104 degrees.

1137
01:06:31,112 --> 01:06:34,448
They couldn't discharge me
because I had an infection.

1138
01:06:34,532 --> 01:06:37,201
They sent me for some urine tests.

1139
01:06:37,284 --> 01:06:39,620
I left the room and told my roommates,

1140
01:06:39,704 --> 01:06:41,580
I had two roommates,

1141
01:06:41,664 --> 01:06:44,667
"Keep an eye on my baby.
I'll be right back."

1142
01:06:45,126 --> 01:06:47,920
The bathroom was just
a few steps from the room.

1143
01:06:48,004 --> 01:06:51,173
-[suspenseful music playing]
-I came back, and my daughter was gone.

1144
01:06:51,257 --> 01:06:55,344
The first thing I thought was,
"Well, maybe they're bathing her,

1145
01:06:55,428 --> 01:06:57,680
-or they took her to feed her."
-[music stops]

1146
01:06:58,347 --> 01:07:00,266
I was sure a nurse had her.

1147
01:07:00,349 --> 01:07:03,436
Never, never did I think
my baby was kidnapped.

1148
01:07:03,519 --> 01:07:06,147
[intriguing music playing]

1149
01:07:29,837 --> 01:07:32,882
I was just told that my baby
was kidnapped from this hospital,

1150
01:07:32,965 --> 01:07:34,508
the General Hospital.

1151
01:07:35,134 --> 01:07:38,095
-I love my baby so much.
