Someone can have these.

1392
01:21:05,193 --> 01:21:07,237
Oh, honey, your treasures.

1393
01:21:07,320 --> 01:21:10,532
My treasures.
You know they're my treasures. [chuckles]

1394
01:21:12,576 --> 01:21:14,995
Does anyone want a picture of my Arturo?

1395
01:21:17,330 --> 01:21:19,583
We can just drag this around. Look.

1396
01:21:19,666 --> 01:21:20,876
Jesus Christ.

1397
01:21:20,959 --> 01:21:23,503
And obviously,
you can take these two, honey.

1398
01:21:23,587 --> 01:21:24,629
Yes.

1399
01:21:24,713 --> 01:21:27,465
-I can’t leave you clothes, but, um…
-No, honey, I know.

1400
01:21:27,549 --> 01:21:30,552
This is enough. You’re leaving me
the most important thing.

1401
01:21:30,635 --> 01:21:32,929
[Alejandra] We’ll all gonna
be fine, you’ll see.

1402
01:21:33,013 --> 01:21:34,347
You'll see.

1403
01:21:34,431 --> 01:21:37,267
-You're the one forging this path.
-[Alejandra] Yes.

1404
01:21:37,350 --> 01:21:40,145
None of us have left yet,
but you're going to be first.

1405
01:21:40,228 --> 01:21:41,980
-[Alejandra] Yes.
-And you'll see.

1406
01:21:42,063 --> 01:21:45,400
-We'll start leaving one after another.
-[Alejandra] I'm opening the door for us.

1407
01:21:45,483 --> 01:21:48,278
-Yes, you are.
-[Alejandra] I’m taking you all with me.

1408
01:21:48,361 --> 01:21:49,362
Yes.

1409
01:21:50,530 --> 01:21:52,782
Don’t stop calling me
or picking up the phone.

1410
01:21:54,159 --> 01:21:56,786
I love you. I love you all so much.

1411
01:21:57,370 --> 01:22:00,832
-I love you. I love you so much.
-[Alejandra] I love you too, Carla.

1412
01:22:03,251 --> 01:22:06,212
[distant people shouting]

1413
01:22:12,135 --> 01:22:14,512
[Alejandra] During these
13 years in prison,

1414
01:22:15,513 --> 01:22:19,100
I have focused on accepting
not being a mom.

1415
01:22:19,601 --> 01:22:23,605
Before, I think my desire to be a mom

1416
01:22:23,688 --> 01:22:26,816
was more about pleasing others.

1417
01:22:28,735 --> 01:22:33,073
But what else is out there
beyond being a mom?

1418
01:22:34,366 --> 01:22:38,620
And finally understood
that there is so much to live for.

1419
01:22:40,121 --> 01:22:42,916
[women chattering]

1420
01:22:44,960 --> 01:22:48,088
You breathe just like that,
just like drinking water.

1421
01:22:49,005 --> 01:22:51,675
-She's so nervous.
-[guard] Wait one moment.

1422
01:22:51,758 --> 01:22:53,510
[Alejandra] I love you all so much.

1423
01:22:53,593 --> 01:22:55,679
[woman] A cheers for Ale.

1424
01:22:55,762 --> 01:22:57,472
[all] Hey!

1425
01:22:57,555 --> 01:23:00,517
One, two, three, Ale!

1426
01:23:00,600 --> 01:23:02,602
-[Alejandra] Thank you, loves.
-[woman] Love you.

1427
01:23:02,686 --> 01:23:04,521
[Alejandra] Thank you for everything.

1428
01:23:04,604 --> 01:23:07,899
-I don't want to leave you guys.
-[Carla] I'm really going to miss you.

1429
01:23:08,525 --> 01:23:12,153
-I love you very much.
-[Alejandra] Stay strong. Stay strong.

1430
01:23:12,237 --> 01:23:13,488
Strong.

1431
01:23:13,989 --> 01:23:15,240
[woman] I love you very much.

1432
01:23:17,784 --> 01:23:19,035
I love you all.

1433
01:23:19,119 --> 01:23:21,496
I'll never forget you, Ale.
I love you, girl.

1434
01:23:21,579 --> 01:23:22,580
Bye.

1435
01:23:25,542 --> 01:23:26,584
[Carla] Bye, Ale.

1436
01:23:28,253 --> 01:23:30,463
[chattering]

1437
01:23:30,547 --> 01:23:32,132
[gentle guitar music playing]

1438
01:23:32,215 --> 01:23:33,425
Oh, there she is!

1439
01:23:33,508 --> 01:23:36,428
[all cheering]

1440
01:23:40,807 --> 01:23:43,351
[Alejandra's mother] Oh, honey, come here.

1441
01:23:45,562 --> 01:23:46,771
We’re here.

1442
01:23:48,064 --> 01:23:49,149
We’re together again.

1443
01:23:49,232 --> 01:23:51,901
-[Alejandra] It’s over.
-[Alejandra's mother] It’s over, my child.

1444
01:23:51,985 --> 01:23:53,194
It's over.

1445
01:23:54,279 --> 01:23:59,284
[Arturo] <i>Alejandra is leaving prison</i>
<i>at 39 years old. She went in at 26.</i>

1446
01:24:00,076 --> 01:24:01,703
My love, I love you.

1447
01:24:01,786 --> 01:24:03,079
Bravo, Arturo!

1448
01:24:07,459 --> 01:24:09,586
[Arturo]
Of all the years we've been married,

1449
01:24:09,669 --> 01:24:11,963
I've lived alone longer than with her.

1450
01:24:15,383 --> 01:24:16,885
And she's not crying, right?

1451
01:24:18,636 --> 01:24:21,306
I’m happy with what I have

1452
01:24:21,389 --> 01:24:24,017
and what we can start over with.

1453
01:24:25,477 --> 01:24:28,271
Obviously, you always have
that nagging feeling

1454
01:24:28,354 --> 01:24:31,066
about having your own kids,

1455
01:24:31,149 --> 01:24:34,652
and if the opportunity arises to, well,

1456
01:24:34,736 --> 01:24:37,030
do IVF and get a surrogate,

1457
01:24:37,113 --> 01:24:38,907
yeah, maybe we will.

1458
01:24:38,990 --> 01:24:42,368
With a child, your last name,
and lineage, continues

1459
01:24:42,452 --> 01:24:44,579
and whatever you want them to carry on.

1460
01:24:45,872 --> 01:24:49,584
I would indeed like to have,
well, a child.

1461
01:24:51,294 --> 01:24:54,714
Not as much as before, but I still have
that desire engrained in me,

1462
01:24:54,798 --> 01:24:56,966
and I don't think it will ever go away.

1463
01:24:57,050 --> 01:24:59,135
[gentle guitar music continues]

1464
01:25:21,116 --> 01:25:22,909
[actress chuckles]

1465
01:25:28,498 --> 01:25:30,667
What do you think ours will be like?

1466
01:25:30,750 --> 01:25:33,128
As long as he doesn't turn out
like that one.

1467
01:25:38,466 --> 01:25:39,801
Is he moving?

1468
01:25:41,886 --> 01:25:43,513
Yeah, our baby just moved.

1469
01:25:44,514 --> 01:25:46,349
What's up, baby?

1470
01:25:46,432 --> 01:25:47,934
My baby son.

1471
01:25:48,768 --> 01:25:50,186
[Arturo chuckles]

1472
01:25:53,857 --> 01:25:55,066
[director] Cut!

1473
01:25:58,111 --> 01:25:59,487
What did you think?

1474
01:26:01,114 --> 01:26:02,365
It's…

1475
01:26:05,326 --> 01:26:06,786
[director] What about you?

1476
01:26:08,246 --> 01:26:09,497
[Arturo] Good, good.

1477
01:26:10,415 --> 01:26:11,583
Let's go.

1478
01:26:16,171 --> 01:26:17,380
[Arturo] Hey.

1479
01:26:17,463 --> 01:26:21,509
[Alejandra] Being a spectator
to my own story was very impactful.

1480
01:26:22,051 --> 01:26:25,930
In real life, I would've loved
to have been able to say,

1481
01:26:26,014 --> 01:26:28,349
"Take 1" or "Take 2,"

1482
01:26:29,142 --> 01:26:31,019
and be able to repeat scenes.

1483
01:26:31,102 --> 01:26:33,188
[director] I totally understand you, Ale.

1484
01:26:33,855 --> 01:26:37,483
And if we could write something
and think up some takes

1485
01:26:37,567 --> 01:26:40,862
or come up with a different ending
for this movie, what would you say?

1486
01:26:40,945 --> 01:26:43,156
If I could write the ending of this movie,

1487
01:26:43,239 --> 01:26:45,617
I think I would go
in a different direction.

1488
01:26:46,534 --> 01:26:48,036
I would keep growing.

1489
01:26:48,536 --> 01:26:50,496
And be able to enjoy myself.

1490
01:26:51,497 --> 01:26:54,751
And I would go…
I would go on a trip, I think.

1491
01:26:56,419 --> 01:27:01,424
To a beach
where I would be very happy and fulfilled.

1492
01:27:01,507 --> 01:27:03,718
[seagulls calling]

1493
01:27:21,945 --> 01:27:25,031
[director] Ale, I would've loved
your ending at the beach.

1494
01:27:25,114 --> 01:27:27,033
That would be a happy ending for me.

1495
01:27:27,533 --> 01:27:29,869
It's been two years
since you came out of prison,

1496
01:27:29,953 --> 01:27:32,413
and a lot has happened since you got out.

1497
01:27:32,497 --> 01:27:34,666
How would you finish the documentary?

1498
01:27:37,502 --> 01:27:39,629
What ending would I show?

1499
01:27:44,717 --> 01:27:45,927
Oh, my.

1500
01:27:46,761 --> 01:27:50,139
Life changes in the blink of an eye.

1501
01:27:50,223 --> 01:27:52,767
[heartfelt music playing]

1502
01:27:54,936 --> 01:27:56,896
When I got out of prison

1503
01:27:57,397 --> 01:28:01,693
Arturo told me again
that he still wanted to be a father.

1504
01:28:01,776 --> 01:28:03,736
And I told him that that was valid

1505
01:28:03,820 --> 01:28:07,156
and that he should go
and find his happiness.

1506
01:28:07,240 --> 01:28:10,118
That I definitely wasn't going
to undergo any treatment,

1507
01:28:10,201 --> 01:28:12,870
and that he wasn't going
to be a father with me.

1508
01:28:12,954 --> 01:28:15,832
We were separated for a while,
gave each other some space,

1509
01:28:15,915 --> 01:28:19,335
and he had another relationship,
a short affair

1510
01:28:19,419 --> 01:28:22,505
that resulted in his son being born.

1511
01:28:24,757 --> 01:28:26,592
Then, Arturo came looking for me.

1512
01:28:26,676 --> 01:28:29,345
We talked, and he told me
everything that had happened.

1513
01:28:29,429 --> 01:28:33,975
He told me that, well that
he missed me a lot, that he loved me,

1514
01:28:34,058 --> 01:28:36,853
and that he wanted me to be in his life.

1515
01:28:37,645 --> 01:28:39,647
That we should try again,

1516
01:28:39,731 --> 01:28:42,025
and I decided to give it a try.

1517
01:28:44,485 --> 01:28:47,196
It makes me very happy to see him smile

1518
01:28:47,280 --> 01:28:49,866
and to see him fulfilled as a father.

1519
01:28:51,242 --> 01:28:53,453
It makes me even happier

1520
01:28:53,536 --> 01:28:56,372
that he sees me in his life as,

1521
01:28:57,206 --> 01:28:59,584
as a mother or parent to his son.

1522
01:28:59,667 --> 01:29:02,837
Oh my goodness! Look at you!

1523
01:29:02,920 --> 01:29:05,423
Look how cute! Come here!

1524
01:29:05,965 --> 01:29:07,675
Run! Run! Run!

1525
01:29:07,759 --> 01:29:09,844
Come get me! Ah! Ah!

1526
01:29:09,927 --> 01:29:12,680
["En Otra Vida"
by Yami Safdie & Lasso playing]

1527
01:29:13,264 --> 01:29:14,307
Come here!

1528
01:29:14,932 --> 01:29:16,517
Ah! There he is!

1529
01:29:16,601 --> 01:29:18,227
I see you!

1530
01:29:22,190 --> 01:29:23,775
You can do it! You can do it!

1531
01:29:23,858 --> 01:29:25,610
Come on, my love, you can do it!

1532
01:29:25,693 --> 01:29:27,195
That's it! That's it!

1533
01:29:30,490 --> 01:29:32,283
Whoo!

1534
01:29:32,367 --> 01:29:34,285
Let's go eat. Shall we?

1535
01:29:36,579 --> 01:29:37,789
Do you want pizza?

1536
01:29:37,872 --> 01:29:40,041
["En Otra Vida" continues]

1537
01:30:13,241 --> 01:30:15,576
["En Otra Vida" continues]

1538
01:31:42,288 --> 01:31:44,248
["En Otra Vida" ends]

1539
01:31:44,332 --> 01:31:46,459
[gentle melodic music playing]

1540
01:32:49,730 --> 01:32:52,441
[music becomes moody]

1541
01:33:58,841 --> 01:34:02,053
[music becomes ethereal]

1542
01:35:53,748 --> 01:35:55,708
[music fades]